[227]={["atomIDs"]={"227:description:1-72","227:description:77-165","227:description:167-176","227:description:178-194","227:objective:1-51"},["opening"]="Sirra found a leatherbound book and directed the inquiry to Althea Ebonlocke. She had been handling the recent trouble associated with Morgan Ladimore and might know what the old account could not explain.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Commander Ebonlocke about Morgan Ladimore.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} consulted Commander Ebonlocke about Morgan Ladimore.",["sourceHash"]="f31c7b445225551cbfb2612859b6ceff48da25c9da3d000ddf66f0b86060c577",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[228]={["atomIDs"]={"228:description:1-129","228:description:131-199","228:objective:1-81"},["opening"]="Ebonlocke's scouts described Mor'Ladim following a meandering route through the cemetery. His burial place lay beyond the house on the hill; the commander asked for his skull when the threat had been confronted.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Mor'Ladim and return his skull to Ebonlocke.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against Mor'Ladim and delivered his skull to Ebonlocke.",["sourceHash"]="f11a2b54fda0646ef6cd1a1d3ce839727b9951e8efc2265c8aad3aec0553aad9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[229]={["atomIDs"]={"229:description:67-180","229:description:182-217","229:description:219-234","229:description:236-266","229:description:268-313","229:objective:1-47"},["bridge"]="The assignment against Mor'Ladim had returned to Ebonlocke. One matter still required care: Sarah Ladimore had survived and served as a Watcher, and the news of her father needed to reach her.",["bridgeFrom"]=228,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Morgan Ladimore's daughter survived. Ebonlocke explained that Sarah was now a Watcher, still troubled by her father's death, and asked that the news be brought to her.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Watcher Sarah Ladimore.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the news to Watcher Sarah Ladimore.",["sourceHash"]="7943ba146402eaf4fcea327fb6d1bcc337ca6b9ceb6add4159e6c2bfe12fd806",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[230]={["atomIDs"]={"230:description:1-63","230:description:68-139","230:objective:1-40"},["opening"]="The hasty mound at Sven's farm had yielded a dirt-stained book without a title. Its contents concerned the man whose family died there, and the book had to be put in Sven's hands.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the book from the farm to Sven.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the book from Sven's farm to him.",["sourceHash"]="9e30ec19cc3c59de4c951e221eb15103c72c4b178bb0a83ddb7f0f971dc3b382",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[231]={["aftermath"]="A voice answered at the grave, recognizing Sarah's survival. Morgan spoke of his burden lifting and his soul finding rest, leaving the sword Archeus for a purpose he believed he had failed.",["atomIDs"]={"231:description:1-40","231:description:51-144","231:description:149-256","231:objective:1-54"},["bridge"]="The news had reached Sarah, but she had a final message for her father. Her ring was to lie on Morgan Ladimore's grave, carrying the hope that he might know she lived and did not blame him.",["bridgeFrom"]=229,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"231:completion:1-39","231:completion:44-54","231:completion:56-61","231:completion:63-92","231:completion:94-135","231:completion:144-166","231:completion:168-221","231:completion:223-348","231:completion:353-367"},["opening"]="Sarah offered her ring for her father's grave. She hoped that somehow he might know she lived and that his family did not hold him responsible for what happened.",["pending"]="{actor} would lay Sarah Ladimore's ring at Morgan's grave.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Sarah Ladimore's ring to Morgan Ladimore's grave.",["sourceHash"]="5a0c561138a012847a1eff664be32c197aceb409bba984be30b99bdad9eb3ba9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[232]={["aftermath"]="Luca prepared a kit while regretting that Zinge had not come herself.",["atomIDs"]={"232:description:1-51","232:description:54-108","232:description:113-156","232:description:158-167","232:description:169-255","232:description:258-293","232:description:296-426","232:description:429-503","232:objective:1-60"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"232:completion:1-32","232:completion:35-115","232:completion:120-159"},["opening"]="Zinge saw potential in Keever's research if a more capable investigator pursued it. A purchase order for a testing kit was the first preparation before she would explain the fieldwork.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to present Zinge's order to Luca.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the purchase order.",["sourceHash"]="0f57d383fbfceeb513bb25a14afce89abc8b5c0aacc25c82e4f56fe7b163689d",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[235]={["atomIDs"]={"235:description:1-29","235:description:32-64","235:description:69-146","235:description:149-251","235:description:254-317","235:description:320-469","235:objective:1-63"},["opening"]="Gorlach directed ambitious hunters north toward the Horde's two Ashenvale outposts. Senani's hunt was the named opportunity for those seeking a test beyond the Barrens.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Senani.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached the hunting guide.",["sourceHash"]="8f201d121f121023b1c307bafc1a5ad6f985e1deb373bc30727d3cd21cff9e6e",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[237]={["atomIDs"]={"237:description:1-73","237:description:76-153","237:description:156-267","237:description:272-372","237:description:375-409","237:description:412-453","237:objective:1-149"},["opening"]="Gravelgaw wanted to maintain pressure until the dwarven troops returned from the Alliance front. Skullthumpers and seers in the southern hills were the next targets in the defense of the Loch.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront ten Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and ten Stonesplinter Seers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Gravelgaw's assignment against the skullthumpers and seers.",["sourceHash"]="ec6e18f252c110b3f42e145af442baad9b54e0aaff37a403312a565ce667a24b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[238]={["aftermath"]="Zinge began adjustments and revealed that the future work would take place in a desert.",["atomIDs"]={"238:description:1-21","238:description:24-89","238:description:92-195","238:description:198-247","238:description:252-280","238:description:283-324","238:objective:1-66"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"238:completion:1-87","238:completion:92-177","238:completion:179-244","238:completion:249-310","238:completion:312-423","238:completion:428-450"},["opening"]="The kit was ready on the Society's tab. Luca sent it back with greetings while Zinge awaited the equipment needed to outline the next task.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the field kit to Zinge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the kit.",["sourceHash"]="b5a14d67c6affdc07972fdec5a5daf62bcd27b6fe5b7f6091060253c7233ee42",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[240]={["atomIDs"]={"240:description:1-41","240:objective:1-44"},["bridge"]="The spider legs had reached Grual, and the cakes were now ready. The work returned from Darkshire's kitchen to the man hiding beyond it: Jitters still needed the meal that had begun the errand.",["bridgeFrom"]=93,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Grual's oddly named cakes were ready. The next journey carried food back to Jitters, whose long seclusion had left little room for decent meals.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the Dusky Crab Cakes to Jitters.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Dusky Crab Cakes to Jitters.",["sourceHash"]="05f73e2b1a2b8cacd480bf4272161a5534fe92a834b46b21413131d18e315221",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[243]={["atomIDs"]={"243:description:1-124","243:description:127-228","243:description:231-284","243:description:289-395","243:description:398-462","243:description:467-508","243:objective:1-99"},["opening"]="Zinge's field test would compare Tanaris basilisk, hyena and scorpid tissues. Before acceptable samples could be processed, the modified kit required a Gadgetzan power source from Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Bilgewhizzle for the testing kit's power source.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle about a power source for the testing kit.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="665c22c5de1cf6a44d1bf7b89d27591a764437bd6fcac09836dda988ba95e676",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[244]={["atomIDs"]={"244:description:1-9","244:description:12-55","244:description:58-150","244:description:155-203","244:description:206-269","244:description:272-330","244:description:335-404","244:objective:1-24"},["opening"]="Parker had seen gnoll camps north and east of his patrol. Though the road was safe for the moment, Lakeshire had to hear of the gathering force through Deputy Feldon.",["pending"]="{actor} would report Parker's sightings to Deputy Feldon.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Parker's report to Deputy Feldon.",["sourceHash"]="83566e642fa42534634ca7ef816f2bb580bbd4674c74dc499fef4ce7f2d0f7ce",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[245]={["atomIDs"]={"245:description:1-9","245:description:11-84","245:description:86-213","245:description:218-295","245:description:297-403","245:description:408-477","245:objective:1-83"},["opening"]="Spiders had overwhelmed the Watch's reach at Duskwood's western border. Dodds had too few people to handle them and warned that their venom added danger to an already difficult patrol.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Dodds' assignment against fifteen Pygmy Venom Web Spiders.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against fifteen Pygmy Venom Web Spiders and reported to Dodds.",["sourceHash"]="90d92964d374715321676b0f89233828b740f780a5358338369b09db63d06dd7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[246]={["atomIDs"]={"246:description:1-93","246:description:98-132","246:description:135-262","246:description:265-337","246:description:342-402","246:objective:1-98"},["opening"]="Feldon lacked spare soldiers but could not ignore the gnoll camps along southern Redridge's road. He called for scouting under pressure: an attack on their mongrels and poachers also had to produce an assessment of the threat.",["pending"]="{actor} would scout the camps and meet Feldon's assignment against ten mongrels and six poachers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Feldon's assignment against the specified gnolls and returned with the report.",["sourceHash"]="aa629a07310211838212dd4a52c0fd25e5f8d51c09dcd886e1c71736ff008cf9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[247]={["aftermath"]="Senani recognized proof that all three beasts of the Ashenvale Hunt had fallen. She commended the hunter's strength and offered a token in acknowledgment of that completed hunt.",["atomIDs"]={"247:completion:1-69","247:completion:71-173","247:completion:175-252","247:completion:257-371","247:completion:373-406"},["availabilityQualification"]={["basis"]="Catalog states positive beta server experience; confirms reported definition, not that a player can reach its giver in the target release",["currentServerPlayableConfirmed"]=false,["eligibility"]="BETA_SERVER_DEFINED_PUBLISHER_CLAIM",["sourceReceipt"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639 ; https://tierhall.app/wow/quests/247"},["completionOnly"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"247:completion:1-69","247:completion:71-173","247:completion:175-252","247:completion:257-371","247:completion:373-406"},["factSourceMetadata"]={["finisherIDs"]={12696},["finisherName"]="Senani Thunderheart",["giverIDs"]={12696},["giverName"]="Senani Thunderheart"},["fieldBlockers"]={"Acceptance description absent.","Acceptance objective absent.","Opening, pending intention, and personal objective discharge remain source-blocked."},["kind"]="COMPLETION_ONLY",["minimumStage"]=4,["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="c5e697cdac45f5cb2fae257ecc4ce8280ece47e6ed7ea18c5971cebc9c7e2d5d",["sourceMapID"]="1440",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[248]={["atomIDs"]={"248:description:1-120","248:description:123-218","248:description:223-319","248:description:324-374","248:description:377-467","248:objective:1-52","248:objective:57-110"},["opening"]="Theocritus detected conflict between Morganth and Stonewatch's orcs without knowing its cause. Another hidden glyph, set high in the intact watchtower beside the keep, might reveal what divided them.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find a discreet container for the Glyph of Azora atop Stonewatch's intact tower.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} placed the Glyph of Azora in a suitable container at the watchtower.",["sourceHash"]="96716abfac3be16fda5a82a813497662be783c8643b83b98af95511e31ab777a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[249]={["atomIDs"]={"249:description:1-59","249:description:64-126","249:description:129-228","249:description:233-319","249:description:322-378","249:description:383-429","249:description:432-474","249:objective:1-16","249:objective:21-101"},["opening"]="Theocritus believed Morganth was searching for the Scythe of Elune and feared he might already had found it. With Redridge and Stormwind threatened by that possibility, the mage called for a confrontation in Ilgalar and the recovery of Morganth's pendant.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Morganth and bring his Pendant of Shadow to Theocritus.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against Morganth and delivered his Pendant of Shadow to Theocritus.",["sourceHash"]="c678aed984412dad316027c5f70ebd91cf4e22386b1eb4b23831731a2d0f8230",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[250]={["atomIDs"]={"250:description:1-69","250:description:72-148","250:description:151-227","250:description:230-327","250:description:332-357","250:description:360-434","250:description:438-480","250:objective:1-152"},["opening"]="The destruction of the Thandol Span and the fall of Dun Modr made Hinderweir fear for Stonewrought Dam. With his security detail depleted, Dark Iron sappers at the eastern ramp demanded investigation.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search the dam's eastern ramp for evidence of the sappers' plans.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search for a clue near the dam's eastern ramp.",["sourceHash"]="a3edade2785198b5582c483e0aecc751d85a3ab3520673bd4ab49b17990b0e3e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[251]={["atomIDs"]={"251:description:1-44","251:description:47-147","251:objective:1-43"},["bridge"]="Abercrombie's letter had reached the mayor, but its language barred understanding. Ello turned to Sirra Von'Indi's knowledge of ancient arts and languages for a translation.",["bridgeFrom"]=160,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Ello sent the letter onward to Sirra Von'Indi. Sirra's learning in languages and ancient arts offered the best chance of making the message intelligible.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the Letter to Ello to Sirra Von'Indi.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} placed the letter in Sirra Von'Indi's hands for translation.",["sourceHash"]="384dd849890773fc8c5447fe48f541dd3b2de7b464e79ca3647eab26634d322f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[252]={["aftermath"]="Ello read the translation and understood the supplied materials as aid to a disaster. His reaction turned the apparently charitable errands into a threat against Darkshire.",["atomIDs"]={"252:description:9-97","252:description:102-151","252:description:156-226","252:objective:1-50"},["bridge"]="The translation was finished, and its meaning alarmed Sirra. If the note spoke truly, Abercrombie had done something terrible; the translated warning had to reach Ello before the feared doom reached Darkshire.",["bridgeFrom"]=401,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"252:completion:1-49","252:completion:51-74","252:completion:79-189","252:completion:194-231"},["opening"]="Sirra feared what the translated note implied about Abercrombie. If its claims were true, he believed something terrible had already begun moving toward Darkshire; the mayor had to see the translation at once.",["pending"]="{actor} would hurry the Translated Letter back to Ello.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Translated Letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke.",["sourceHash"]="eae69e958546389c1699f9c138c0d5df2e7185e9cdb6f6f23a92b63777ff8feb",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[253]={["aftermath"]="Ello regarded the recovered heart's magic as a defense against the Embalmer. His account offered Darkshire a means of protection rather than a claim that every danger in its woods had ended.",["atomIDs"]={"253:description:1-61","253:description:64-133","253:description:136-229","253:description:234-343","253:description:348-370","253:description:373-455","253:description:458-494","253:objective:1-19","253:objective:22-91"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"253:completion:1-15","253:completion:17-134","253:completion:139-185","253:completion:187-230"},["opening"]="Ello recounted the children's tale of the Embalmer, an alchemist who placed his heart in his dead wife Eliza to restore her. The story said the act revived her with a hunger for human flesh. Ello now sought that beating heart as the means to break the Embalmer's power.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find Eliza's grave and bring the Embalmer's Heart to Ello.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} retrieved the Embalmer's Heart from Eliza and delivered it to Ello Ebonlocke.",["sourceHash"]="599d2ea4ad5c2233466974e63f3164881afb0a39dbd98186f0e3640724169f1c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[255]={["atomIDs"]={"255:description:1-144","255:description:146-258","255:description:263-292","255:description:294-314","255:description:319-332","255:description:334-360","255:description:362-423","255:description:425-485","255:objective:1-117"},["opening"]="Bluntnose faced months of delay before Ironforge's soldiers could reach Thelsamar. With the town, excavation and dam exposed, he hired help against the Mo'grosh ogres camped northeast of the lake.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Bluntnose's assignment against four ogres, four brutes and four enforcers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the hired assignment against the three specified groups of Mo'grosh ogres.",["sourceHash"]="c28d3a52ee25e4f020b61af2b064cc6c99b550dc7aa7f295efbc485e1266c3e1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[256]={["atomIDs"]={"256:description:1-40","256:description:45-233","256:description:238-336","256:description:341-425","256:objective:1-70"},["opening"]="Thelsamar's warrant named Chok'sul as the presumed coordinator of attacks on the town, dam and excavation. Last seen at the northeastern ogre camp, he was wanted dead, with proof due to Bluntnose.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Chok'sul and take his head to Bluntnose.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the warrant against Chok'sul and delivered his head to Bluntnose.",["sourceHash"]="46845441f61507acc433b28729accdaa7055be50930b86da3439f06f6887b04c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[257]={["atomIDs"]={"257:description:1-50","257:description:52-70","257:description:72-114","257:description:116-229","257:description:234-283","257:description:285-334","257:description:336-423","257:description:428-460","257:description:465-507","257:objective:1-101"},["opening"]="At the Farstrider Lodge, Daryl turned hunting into a boastful contest. Six Mountain Buzzards had to be accounted for within fifteen minutes if his challenger was to meet the wager.",["pending"]="{actor} would attempt Daryl's timed challenge against six Mountain Buzzards.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met Daryl's challenge against six Mountain Buzzards and returned within fifteen minutes.",["sourceHash"]="5e000e97fe9a1b4e066cd82def054250754d5b19cb11f555c7dc501dbb383735",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[258]={["atomIDs"]={"258:description:1-13","258:description:15-87","258:description:89-129","258:description:134-174","258:description:176-260","258:description:262-305","258:description:310-336","258:description:338-389","258:description:394-463","258:description:469-491","258:objective:1-104"},["opening"]="Daryl set a shorter clock for the next hunt: twelve minutes for five Elder Mountain Boars. He warned that these were no easy Coldridge quarry, even as his talk drifted toward the story of his scar.",["pending"]="{actor} would attempt Daryl's twelve-minute boar challenge.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met the challenge against five Elder Mountain Boars and returned to Daryl in time.",["sourceHash"]="c88e9dd39b1ec9b15625a80a7ef34f5d4393ab7024d1d9e5383f44f2d9444a29",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[262]={["atomIDs"]={"262:description:1-85","262:description:140-171","262:description:174-208","262:description:213-308","262:description:311-374","262:objective:1-77"},["opening"]="Sven wanted to identify the stranger he saw after his family's deaths. The book found at the farm was his only fresh lead; someone in Darkshire might recognize it or its owner.",["pending"]="{actor} would show the book to Darkshire's townsfolk.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the book to Madame Eva as part of the search.",["sourceHash"]="7eef34508fe20176b0d2deaf561a60626223f73c06c84b3c656acc443cde059c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[263]={["atomIDs"]={"263:description:1-61","263:description:64-97","263:description:100-142","263:description:145-216","263:description:219-285","263:description:290-363","263:description:366-423","263:objective:1-125"},["opening"]="The reserves had been called away, and Wallbang saw no easing of the trogg incursion. He directed the next effort against Stonesplinter shaman and bonesnappers, ten of each.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Wallbang's assignment against the shaman and bonesnappers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Wallbang's assignment against ten Stonesplinter Shaman and ten Stonesplinter Bonesnappers.",["sourceHash"]="f7c6359cfc5cb537ed68b9c4aad6a80c9e5868c477c1446bb2c8c30d65e43368",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[264]={["aftermath"]="The gemstone dulled, and a cool breeze passed over the briefly silent Sepulcher.",["atomIDs"]={"264:description:1-12","264:description:14-44","264:description:46-137","264:description:142-172","264:description:174-188","264:description:190-241","264:description:243-276","264:description:281-324","264:description:326-388","264:description:393-456","264:description:458-496","264:description:498-504","264:objective:1-54"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"264:completion:1-107","264:completion:112-248","264:completion:250-330","264:completion:332-376"},["opening"]="Clarice resented being placed behind Yuriv's crusade, even before death separated them. Now undead herself, she wanted no further claim on his memory and sent the pendant to his grave.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to place the pendant on Yuriv's tomb.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} laid Clarice's pendant at the tomb.",["sourceHash"]="9ac151a0dafbb95c4477306e7f6a4fe44abda88ac7d3d08038e4d91b83d0562f",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[265]={["atomIDs"]={"265:description:1-67","265:description:70-134","265:description:139-265","265:objective:1-59"},["opening"]="Madame Eva returned the book with a distinction: its author was a stranger to Darkshire, but the book itself was bought in town. The search turned from the traveler's origin to the people who might remember the sale.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask other townsfolk about the book's owner.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} pursued the book's local connection with Clerk Daltry.",["sourceHash"]="85d8b47904b131eb83c6988957d8091a07c79c33711222f9dda7756e85a852f7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[266]={["atomIDs"]={"266:description:1-53","266:description:58-105","266:description:108-194","266:objective:1-50"},["opening"]="Daltry suggested the inn as the next place to ask. A traveler who spent time in Darkshire might have needed a room, and an innkeeper could remember what the registry could not supply.",["pending"]="{actor} would inquire at the inn about the shadowy figure.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the search for the book's owner to Tavernkeep Smitts.",["sourceHash"]="467b7c31a06b92e5fa321ef6ca9a83f2d7fa03922ad8bf2701841b73f1839863",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[267]={["atomIDs"]={"267:description:1-79","267:description:82-223","267:description:226-327","267:description:332-405","267:description:408-463","267:description:466-508","267:objective:1-75"},["opening"]="Rugelfuss could not leave the gate undefended while Ironforge's reserves served at the front. Pressure on the troggs in the hills had to come from outside his regiment, with eight stone teeth brought back as evidence.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain eight Trogg Stone Teeth for Rugelfuss.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered eight Trogg Stone Teeth to Captain Rugelfuss.",["sourceHash"]="a8f9d29a72a8d135144bdc1a9002886aa87ca05cf879fcb7f5715c90e6daa79c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[268]={["aftermath"]="The fuller journal directed Sven's pursuit toward the Dark Riders. He recalled seeing them speak with Morbent Fel at Forlorn Rowe, bringing a named wizard into the account.",["atomIDs"]={"268:description:1-42","268:description:45-97","268:description:109-142","268:description:145-194","268:description:199-351","268:objective:1-47"},["bridge"]="The search for the book's owner had reached Jitters. He now offered the completed journal, willing to surrender his companion of the past weeks if it spared him facing Sven's anger himself.",["bridgeFrom"]=453,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"268:completion:1-82","268:completion:84-195"},["opening"]="Jitters offered the completed journal rather than face Sven himself. The book abandoned at the farm was only half finished; this fuller account might explain more of the killings and the witness who fled them.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry Jitters' completed journal to Sven.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Jitters' completed journal to Sven.",["sourceHash"]="d16f664d2e8c6282fc906f24f24a4833dea8c3786a40601e6e4856c403665d4b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[269]={["aftermath"]="Farthing read the journal and warned of enchantments protecting Morbent Fel from physical attack. The challenge now required a weapon capable of answering those defenses.",["atomIDs"]={"269:description:1-85","269:description:88-155","269:description:160-240","269:description:243-283","269:objective:1-64"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"269:completion:1-54","269:completion:59-134","269:completion:136-191","269:completion:196-392","269:completion:394-482"},["opening"]="The path against Morbent Fel led to Stormwind's Cathedral of Light. Sven trusted Bishop Farthing's wisdom despite the city's abandonment of Darkshire and sent Jitters' journal as evidence of the danger.",["pending"]="{actor} would present Jitters' completed journal to Bishop Farthing.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} gave Bishop Farthing the journal and the account of the threat.",["sourceHash"]="ffded87ff5caf2ba328fa24948926ace1a87ed47e87e6d73ba3c39cee8f2ac7e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[270]={["atomIDs"]={"270:description:1-141","270:description:144-189","270:description:194-272","270:description:275-339","270:description:344-418","270:description:421-478","270:objective:1-71"},["bridge"]="Farthing's warning about Morbent Fel's protections had given the search a new requirement. Lightforge Iron, lost with the Third Fleet, might supply it; Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil was the colleague who could direct the recovery.",["bridgeFrom"]=269,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Farthing knew a metal suited to the struggle against Morbent Fel: Lightforge Iron, lost aboard a ship of the doomed Third Fleet off the Wetlands. Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil Harbor might know where the cargo lay.",["pending"]="{actor} would consult Glorin Steelbrow in Menethil Harbor.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Farthing's inquiry about Lightforge Iron to Glorin Steelbrow.",["sourceHash"]="13fe7c5b0da40654d202886d1dbef1799e8ce62369d65025dd9d22b1730bb23d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[271]={["atomIDs"]={"271:description:1-73","271:description:75-121","271:description:126-241","271:description:243-290","271:description:292-357","271:description:362-429","271:description:434-511","271:objective:1-87"},["opening"]="Vyrin offered an answer to Daryl's boasting. Ol' Sooty, the bear that left the hunter scarred, still laired in the hills over Thelsamar; she thought showing Daryl proof of the bear's defeat might quiet him.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Ol' Sooty and show the evidence to Daryl.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against Ol' Sooty and showed the proof to Daryl.",["sourceHash"]="c58369da9e18e0e5a6d4640c941bea5b9929ceec41cf162274f46ae3d173f21c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[273]={["atomIDs"]={"273:description:1-63","273:description:65-184","273:description:189-295","273:description:300-373","273:objective:1-18"},["opening"]="Huldar's supply party had already set out along the Loch's southern curve. Jern believed the weight of the barrels would keep Miran and Saean from getting far before a traveler could catch them.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find Huldar on the excavation route.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} caught up with Huldar on the supply route.",["sourceHash"]="c09355419f14fbf1750b6605c082108966d7acf1404d3a40245adb4d7f3ef3f0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[274]={["atomIDs"]={"274:description:1-36","274:description:39-71","274:description:74-96","274:description:99-155","274:description:158-186","274:description:189-250","274:description:255-403","274:description:406-446","274:objective:1-103"},["opening"]="Stonesmirk identified Seaforium by its crystals and smell. Water made the powder dangerously reactive, but he named a four-part mixture that could neutralize it; Hinderweir had to hear this discovery quickly.",["pending"]="{actor} would report the Seaforium finding and disarming formula to Hinderweir.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Stonesmirk's discovery back to Chief Engineer Hinderweir.",["sourceHash"]="9bc79e1acf57e5bf668641ec3dfc963eb9ee73bd0179968e472e0bd6229b32bc",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[275]={["atomIDs"]={"275:description:1-61","275:description:64-87","275:description:90-233","275:description:238-299","275:objective:1-76"},["opening"]="Fen Creepers had risen among the waterways, and Rethiel saw them as signs of a sickness in the Wetlands. He did not know its cause, but called for eight creepers to be returned to the marsh.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Rethiel's assignment against eight Fen Creepers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against eight Fen Creepers and returned to Rethiel.",["sourceHash"]="c85ecff37b7e4e9daa68215ded2ede0de46428da7a8282c28a3495a0e3e7189d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[276]={["atomIDs"]={"276:description:1-98","276:description:101-210","276:description:215-258","276:description:261-316","276:description:321-369","276:description:372-426","276:description:429-460","276:objective:1-105"},["opening"]="Rethiel remembered years of peaceful Mosshide life in the Wetlands. Their growing numbers now trampled the fen and consumed too much wood; he demanded a reduction near Algaz to restore the land's balance.",["pending"]="{actor} would meet Rethiel's assignment against fifteen Mosshide Gnolls and ten Mosshide Mongrels.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Rethiel's assignment against the specified Mosshide gnolls and mongrels.",["sourceHash"]="47a6a18339f508793955e41700f5be1e574b4357f3ead9bbd5a80a347b51b4db",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[277]={["atomIDs"]={"277:description:1-105","277:description:108-141","277:description:146-218","277:description:221-315","277:objective:1-45"},["opening"]="The Mosshides' fires wounded Rethiel through the trees cut to feed them. He targeted the flints that made those fires possible, requesting nine from the larger members of the tribe.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather nine Crude Flints for Rethiel.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered nine Crude Flints to Rethiel the Greenwarden.",["sourceHash"]="2c292d4cd315d296da3d592c4b255fb71d4d4ff946741650b0a1779f35dd022f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[278]={["atomIDs"]={"278:description:1-57","278:description:60-125","278:description:128-178","278:description:181-237","278:description:240-319","278:description:324-375","278:description:378-460","278:objective:1-101"},["opening"]="Hinderweir called for the materials to prepare a defense against Seaforium. Venom and a crocolisk tear could be found around the Loch, while the rarer Mo'grosh crystal had to come from the northeastern ogres.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather Lurker Venom, a Mo'grosh Crystal and a Crocolisk Tear.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Hinderweir with the three requested disarming ingredients.",["sourceHash"]="b46cd2afbb602d7dccc6f14276fbce5b26eebee3a297d76977b1da4327fc5201",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[279]={["atomIDs"]={"279:description:1-91","279:description:94-158","279:description:163-331","279:description:334-395","279:description:400-444","279:description:447-492","279:objective:1-25","279:objective:30-60","279:objective:65-118"},["opening"]="Bluegill murlocs threatened Menethil's fishers and merchants from their coastal huts. Boran singled out Gobbler, who raided the road and retreated to the inlet north of town.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront twelve Bluegill Murlocs and Gobbler, bringing Gobbler's head to Boran.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Bluegill assignment and delivered Gobbler's Head to Karl Boran.",["sourceHash"]="37ce3b4ced8a78466e3bdf0b724f638f3f6e7ee7e0c5be280f371c7a0dba7018",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[280]={["aftermath"]="The keg gave a slight fizz as the mixture settled inside. That was the observed response preserved in the source, without a wider claim about the dam's lasting security.",["atomIDs"]={"280:description:1-91","280:description:94-135","280:description:138-233","280:description:236-299","280:description:302-313","280:description:318-399","280:description:402-407","280:objective:1-153"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"280:completion:1-61"},["opening"]="Dark Iron insurgents had been seen swimming toward the dam with a keg. Hinderweir feared the Seaforium was already planted below the water and combined the ingredients into a mixture that had to reach it before the explosion.",["pending"]="{actor} would locate the keg at the dam's base and stir in the Disarming Mixture.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the disarming assignment at the powder keg beneath the dam.",["sourceHash"]="481cab329964a795e77e202b6d5e22e590986e25d85a6547af634b7f427403d1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[281]={["atomIDs"]={"281:description:1-74","281:description:77-224","281:description:227-259","281:description:264-349","281:description:352-399","281:objective:1-58"},["opening"]="Murlocs raided the Blind Princess without sinking her, dragging valuable cargo into the sea. Boran particularly wanted a statuette of Terenas Menethil recovered from the crates and barrels around their coastal camps.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search the coastal murloc cargo for the Menethil Statuette.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assigned search among the coastal murloc crates and barrels.",["sourceHash"]="f6cf918bcce595d9fb6943ddd95e33db2bea032d484bfe0472d7f15de549facf",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[283]={["aftermath"]="Hinderweir credited the report with saving the Stonewrought Dam. His relief carried a limit: he considered it safe for the time being.",["atomIDs"]={"283:description:1-25","283:objective:1-44","283:objective:47-106"},["availabilityQualification"]={["basis"]="Catalog states positive beta server experience; confirms reported definition, not that a player can reach its giver in the target release",["currentServerPlayableConfirmed"]=false,["eligibility"]="BETA_SERVER_DEFINED_PUBLISHER_CLAIM",["sourceReceipt"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639 ; https://tierhall.app/wow/quests/283 ; https://warcraftforever.games/quests/283 ; https://wowfwiki.com/wiki/Quests"},["bridge"]="The mixture had settled into the powder keg with a slight fizz. Its apparent success still had to be carried back to Hinderweir, whose work could not end on an unseen response beneath the dam.",["bridgeFrom"]=280,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"283:completion:1-23","283:completion:25-60","283:completion:62-161","283:completion:163-221","283:completion:226-252","283:completion:258-285"},["opening"]="The mixture had produced a slight fizz in the keg, suggesting that the disarming attempt had worked. Hinderweir still needed a report from the dam's base.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to report the keg's response to Chief Engineer Hinderweir.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the apparent success of the Disarming Mixture to Chief Engineer Hinderweir.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="597c9ee0376bf595b6721f48ac0537004c06ca9ba9d411a547f55d8199c1488d",["sourceMapID"]="1432",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[284]={["atomIDs"]={"284:description:1-97","284:description:102-186","284:objective:1-34"},["opening"]="The searched cluster of huts held no trace of the statuette. Two more hovels to the north and northeast might supply the missing lead.",["pending"]="{actor} would continue searching the northern and northeastern hovels for the statuette.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the next search in the murloc hovels.",["sourceHash"]="bdc8a3a7da35252f16842b8f7c76a718b6d6383fdfe1f484da6878ccb0c7c821",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[285]={["atomIDs"]={"285:description:1-77","285:description:82-148","285:description:153-216","285:objective:1-64"},["opening"]="Another group of huts had yielded nothing. The search narrowed to the hovels farther north, where the missing Menethil Statuette might still be hidden.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search the remaining northern hovels for the statuette.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the further search for the Menethil Statuette.",["sourceHash"]="8bc84b8c90b1f49259eb4f789d8f564e381d0e0036f0ec776b0bdde9c7e2848a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[286]={["aftermath"]="Boran regarded the recovered statuette as the return of precious cargo to the Blind Princess. The salvage had reached the merchant purpose that first sent the search to the hovels.",["atomIDs"]={"286:description:1-109","286:description:112-172","286:description:177-212","286:description:215-270","286:objective:1-40"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"286:completion:1-98","286:completion:100-155","286:completion:160-244"},["opening"]="A barrel freed from the muck contained a silver figurine nestled in fine straw. Its raised hammer identified the sought statuette, ready to be taken back to Boran in Menethil.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return the Menethil Statuette to Boran.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Menethil Statuette to Karl Boran.",["sourceHash"]="ca14bc2c0adfeb65b490b7c1b3b5a50717e48daf338c297dfbd57db0d7c33583",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[288]={["atomIDs"]={"288:description:1-90","288:description:93-109","288:description:112-181","288:description:184-210","288:description:215-319","288:description:322-367","288:description:372-405","288:description:408-492","288:objective:1-44"},["opening"]="Fitzsimmons recounted the Third Fleet's destruction by orc-controlled red dragons off the coast. Claiming to be its sole survivor, he needed a fresh drink before continuing the tale of the sunken ships.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Fitzsimmons a Flagon of Mead.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied First Mate Fitzsimmons with a Flagon of Mead.",["sourceHash"]="896815493d230e088a634aab4679d887b048e1036ce2ee5761d1993970a8628b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[289]={["atomIDs"]={"289:description:1-46","289:description:51-151","289:description:154-257","289:description:260-423","289:description:428-507","289:objective:1-64","289:objective:67-136"},["opening"]="Fitzsimmons said survival had not been granted to his shipmates, only a terrible form of continued existence. A hidden treasure kept their souls in the wrecks, and he hoped an assault on the cursed crew could begin breaking its hold.",["pending"]="{actor} would meet the cursed-crew assignment and return Snellig's Snuffbox.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against thirteen Cursed Sailors, five Cursed Marines and Snellig, delivering the snuffbox to Fitzsimmons.",["sourceHash"]="0d9c72cb9424b2ceec37e2b10ecb7467a0791297a296dc4c33b39aa4a92d794e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[290]={["aftermath"]="The old key fitted the Intrepid's lock despite its rust. The strongbox was accessible, while the nature and cleansing of its contents remained to be addressed.",["atomIDs"]={"290:description:1-111","290:description:114-241","290:description:246-282","290:description:285-329","290:description:332-397","290:description:402-488","290:objective:1-53","290:objective:58-109"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"290:completion:1-46"},["opening"]="Fitzsimmons believed the hidden cargo had to be retrieved and cleansed to free the fleet. Captain Halyndor still haunted the Intrepid and held the key to the strongbox where the unknown object was secured.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain Halyndor's key and open the Intrepid's Locked Strongbox.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the key-and-strongbox assignment aboard the Intrepid.",["sourceHash"]="8bb517c63dd76436136e2a6b1de236a218b0ce397d52ca27f5dff6e2603ee808",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[291]={["atomIDs"]={"291:description:1-10","291:description:12-52","291:description:54-127","291:description:129-191","291:description:196-227","291:description:229-373","291:description:378-439","291:description:441-501","291:objective:1-62"},["opening"]="Senir sent his report to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge's royal chamber. He cautioned against the senator's sour manner and would prefer his own need for assistance left unmentioned.",["pending"]="{actor} would deliver Senir's report to Senator Redstone.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Senir's report to Senator Barin Redstone in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="caae904c2c869416241c609791c171856373be473c302a1f4911fde40346a2e5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[292]={["atomIDs"]={"292:description:1-71","292:description:74-143","292:description:148-236","292:description:239-276","292:objective:1-51"},["opening"]="The opened strongbox held a blackened orb with an eerie pulse. Identified as a Cursed Eye of Paleth, the treasure had to reach Glorin Steelbrow so its curse could be examined.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the Cursed Eye of Paleth to Glorin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Cursed Eye of Paleth to Glorin Steelbrow.",["sourceHash"]="2b87361234444d77f6bd43a65e8ea84546a57997372f614982341f645ef4903d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[293]={["aftermath"]="Benedictus recognized the Eye's sorrowful history and offered to cleanse it. He warned that the powers of such priest-made objects became dangerous when tainted.",["atomIDs"]={"293:description:1-46","293:description:49-155","293:description:158-190","293:description:193-242","293:description:245-256","293:description:261-282","293:objective:1-53","293:objective:56-121"},["bridge"]="The Eye of Paleth had reached Glorin, who could not cleanse it. He traced the Eyes to human priests and sent the cursed orb onward to Benedictus at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light.",["bridgeFrom"]=292,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"293:completion:1-17","293:completion:19-112","293:completion:117-243"},["opening"]="Glorin could not lift the Eye's curse. Because human priests crafted the Eyes of Paleth, he sent the orb to Archbishop Benedictus at Stormwind's Cathedral of Light in hope of stronger help.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry the Cursed Eye of Paleth to Benedictus.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Cursed Eye of Paleth to Archbishop Benedictus.",["sourceHash"]="33664d152f405e184e5a43fa92b6e3a2a11afeeae13ba547d7a0d338a2e969b4",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[294]={["atomIDs"]={"294:description:1-47","294:description:50-104","294:description:107-200","294:description:205-249","294:description:252-323","294:description:326-353","294:description:358-424","294:objective:1-110"},["opening"]="Ormer said the excavated bones drew raptors to Whelgar's dig, killing workers and trapping the survivors above it. He began his demanded revenge with mottled raptors and screechers west of the bluff.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Ormer's assignment against ten Mottled Raptors and ten Mottled Screechers.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Ormer's assignment against the mottled raptors and screechers.",["sourceHash"]="8ed00f1084bab112c18343b0ba760447bfe0f04b9c80eee17a6f0e3ad49f86c7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[295]={["atomIDs"]={"295:description:1-77","295:description:80-157","295:description:160-213","295:objective:1-146"},["opening"]="Ormer's attention turned below the refuge to the Scytheclaws and Razormaws. He called for ten of each as the next part of his revenge for the ruined excavation.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront ten Mottled Scytheclaws and ten Mottled Razormaws for Ormer.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Ormer's assignment against ten Scytheclaws and ten Razormaws.",["sourceHash"]="838f04860d676233e01bc57068d258c6bbb9265fd87155b85c5b2ed0eb331ca6",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[296]={["aftermath"]="Ormer remembered the workers who had died while simply doing their jobs. He treated the reprisal as a warning to future attackers, not the restoration of those lives.",["atomIDs"]={"296:description:1-96","296:description:99-130","296:description:133-215","296:description:220-255","296:description:258-304","296:description:307-382","296:description:385-433","296:objective:1-143"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"296:completion:1-14","296:completion:16-55","296:completion:57-121","296:completion:123-253"},["opening"]="A larger raptor had caught Ormer's eye. He suspected Sarltooth led the others to the dig and demanded the beast's death, with a talon returned as proof.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Sarltooth and take a talon to Ormer.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Sarltooth and returned a talon to Ormer.",["sourceHash"]="d86e79932dea5ffbdc6ccd115131703ed661c7f72737517c4d4ba93cec0d0910",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[297]={["atomIDs"]={"297:description:1-116","297:description:119-235","297:description:238-289","297:description:292-316","297:description:321-396","297:description:399-454","297:objective:1-42"},["opening"]="Carved idols emerged shortly before troggs drove the excavators from the ruins. Fellhew said the objects sent the troggs berserk and wanted eight recovered both for study and to remove them from their hands.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover eight Carved Stone Idols for Fellhew.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered eight Carved Stone Idols to Magmar Fellhew.",["sourceHash"]="80ec90e28c6f87597b10880935b6553e9c028929170f3281e6172603447132f0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[298]={["atomIDs"]={"298:description:1-117","298:description:120-137","298:description:140-164","298:description:167-202","298:description:207-253","298:objective:1-63"},["opening"]="Ironband's progress report carried another request for blastpowder. Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar was the excavation's local contact and the first destination for the paperwork.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry Ironband's Progress Report to Jern.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Ironband's Progress Report to Jern Hornhelm.",["sourceHash"]="198d0d00972f17cccf0c4b71b32c9babf865e24f06a5b37b50fa5837ecf195d9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[299]={["aftermath"]="With the stone whole, Whelgar could resume the Titan-script translation. Its newly readable references to Old Gods chained beneath the land widened the mystery beyond the ruined dig.",["atomIDs"]={"299:description:1-74","299:description:77-119","299:description:122-180","299:description:185-218","299:description:221-267","299:description:270-288","299:description:293-388","299:description:391-454","299:description:457-510","299:objective:1-129"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"299:completion:1-30","299:completion:32-45","299:completion:47-63","299:completion:65-134","299:completion:136-168","299:completion:170-173","299:completion:177-201","299:completion:205-272"},["opening"]="Whelgar's translated Goaz Stone broke off in four places amid references to a divine plan and a doomed prophecy. Raptors prevented the old prospector from searching for the missing fragments himself.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to seek the Ados, Modr, Golm and Neru tablet fragments at the excavation.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the four missing tablet fragments to Prospector Whelgar.",["sourceHash"]="ca4232225f3c3ea2b04c21b4d7c48ed37eb2c961b6abebf0e4fde58dc366e593",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[301]={["atomIDs"]={"301:description:1-53","301:description:55-136","301:description:141-158","301:description:160-238","301:description:240-333","301:description:338-388","301:objective:1-56"},["opening"]="More blastpowder required approval from Ironforge. Jern sent the excavation report to Prospector Stormpike at the Explorers' League, warning that the site's slow progress might provoke him.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take Ironband's Progress Report to Prospector Stormpike.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Ironband's Progress Report to Prospector Stormpike.",["sourceHash"]="455234f6c5e89e7dcddda93689707e0aad3bee7b9abe0a725f90eae5b18c044a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[302]={["atomIDs"]={"302:description:1-65","302:description:68-143","302:description:146-209","302:description:214-314","302:description:317-380","302:objective:1-38"},["opening"]="Stormpike had sent approval for Ironband's supplies ahead to Thelsamar. A missing previous shipment made the next delivery a matter for personal oversight, beginning with Jern Hornhelm.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Jern about the approved supply shipment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Jern Hornhelm about the shipment for Ironband.",["sourceHash"]="0591983784c1d99a11589cab694fca34739779964e1e039dc366cd3ecc695297",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[303]={["atomIDs"]={"303:description:1-31","303:description:34-199","303:description:202-237","303:description:240-264","303:description:269-320","303:description:323-460","303:description:465-479","303:objective:1-145"},["opening"]="The Dark Irons had broken the Thandol Span and taken Dun Modr while dwarven troops fought abroad. Garmason needed pressure on their fighters and specialists long enough for the reserves to arrive.",["pending"]="{actor} would undertake Garmason's assignment against the specified Dark Iron forces.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against ten Dark Iron Dwarves and five each of the Tunnelers, Saboteurs and Demolitionists.",["sourceHash"]="df4d3eeac3bd68d405fd29ef020fa05118d0c577d4d50ceb058bc86f448b1901",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[304]={["atomIDs"]={"304:description:1-51","304:description:53-133","304:description:136-183","304:description:186-298","304:description:300-418","304:description:423-488","304:description:490-511","304:objective:1-83"},["opening"]="Longbraid lost soldiers at Dun Modr and his brother at the bridge. Roggo's information named Balgaras the Foul as the local Dark Iron leader, hiding on Direforge Hill while others fought for him.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Balgaras and bring his ear to Longbraid.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Balgaras the Foul and delivered his ear to Longbraid.",["sourceHash"]="6331ad2e11c65eb84d1d1e311382d73afd33414fbe340bf5e57082ea04f9a4e1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[305]={["atomIDs"]={"305:description:1-58","305:description:61-103","305:description:108-181","305:description:184-226","305:description:229-291","305:description:294-319","305:description:324-425","305:description:428-458","305:description:461-507","305:objective:1-91"},["opening"]="Tarrel's wife Merrin had stopped sending her weekly letters from Whelgar's excavation. Nearly two silent weeks had made him fear for the team, and he asked that contact be restored.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find Merrin Rockweaver at the excavation.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} contacted Merrin Rockweaver at the excavation site.",["sourceHash"]="b9b06f9f2744d8607af04de591a7aef62d747f16195056d778ee3777635fc828",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[306]={["atomIDs"]={"306:description:1-16","306:description:19-100","306:description:105-186","306:description:189-209","306:description:214-267","306:description:270-306","306:description:309-327","306:description:330-360","306:description:365-409","306:description:412-448","306:objective:1-47"},["opening"]="Merrin described raptors overwhelming the dig after workers uncovered large bones. Ormer saved her and the prospector, but they remained trapped; a note could at least tell Tarrel what had happened.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return Merrin's note to Tarrel.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Merrin's note to Tarrel Rockweaver.",["sourceHash"]="e4099c648f842c3d0cf294c62184f186e6a27a4ca6ea7ed120d62311e705f835",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[307]={["atomIDs"]={"307:description:1-52","307:description:55-195","307:description:200-354","307:description:357-417","307:description:422-485","307:description:488-497","307:objective:1-65","307:objective:70-101"},["opening"]="The exhausted Silver Stream Mine became a Miners' League storehouse before kobolds occupied it. Stormpike wanted the League's equipment retrieved before the soldiers entered and risk breaking it in the fighting.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover four loads of Miners' Gear from the mine's crates.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned four loads of Miners' Gear to Mountaineer Stormpike.",["sourceHash"]="dba753abe09b8286207d47bb03f19a6869b0ffb3f1088209633d02007b89372d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[308]={["atomIDs"]={"308:requestItems:1-5","308:requestItems:7-40","308:requestItems:42-82","308:requestItems:84-177"},["coverageQualification"]="BASIC_RETAINED_EXCHANGE_CONTEXT",["minimumStage"]=3,["objectiveSummary"]="Bring Thunder Ale to Jarven Thunderbrew.",["opening"]="Jarven guarded a cellar full of drink under orders not to touch it. What tempted him was a taste of Thunder Ale brought from elsewhere.",["pending"]="{actor} would bring Thunder Ale to Jarven.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Jarven with Thunder Ale.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_SOURCE_REVIEWED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_CERTIFIED",["sourceHash"]="895b177ad7dc4c361760496433aa7c666c9411b25475cf32a8390b8b05cb0a9f",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639",["unresolvedFields"]={"currentPlayability","unlistedQuantities"}},
[309]={["atomIDs"]={"309:description:1-16","309:description:21-66","309:description:68-202","309:description:207-251","309:objective:1-93"},["opening"]="Miran was ready to shoulder the powder for Ironband, but the road remained dangerous. The possibility of further Dark Iron interference made an escort valuable all the way to the excavation.",["pending"]="{actor} would protect Miran and the shipment on the journey to Ironband.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the escort of Miran and the shipment to the excavation and informed Ironband.",["sourceHash"]="1c2860301e99523b992389705070ac4654761a12c6d22150c2f7ea0d0c5335fc",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[311]={["atomIDs"]={"311:description:1-139","311:objective:1-78"},["opening"]="A barrel of Thunder Ale was to serve as evidence that Marleth's Scalder was placed in the Kharanos distillery cellar. The barrel now had to travel back to Marleth Barleybrew in Brewnall Village.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring the Thunder Ale barrel to Marleth.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the barrel of Thunder Ale to Marleth Barleybrew.",["sourceHash"]="d04fd871f302b8a94ed2571e0cfc21d8ef46efdfb6d4482a40754d342debd0e5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[312]={["atomIDs"]={"312:description:1-80","312:description:83-126","312:description:129-218","312:description:221-274","312:description:277-321","312:description:326-362","312:description:365-398","312:description:401-481","312:objective:1-90"},["opening"]="Old Icebeard carried off MacGrann's locked winter meat supply while the dwarf was hunting. The thorium locker might still protect the food, but MacGrann's injured leg prevented a quick recovery from the beast's cave.",["pending"]="{actor} would retrieve MacGrann's dried meats from Old Icebeard's cave.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} recovered Tundra MacGrann's dried meats from the stolen locker.",["sourceHash"]="9d7163773302fedd50413b151714cfba4e9a4a9f947cb1be1443a5de391fc767",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[313]={["atomIDs"]={"313:description:1-42","313:description:45-106","313:description:109-122","313:description:125-142","313:description:145-167","313:description:172-239","313:description:242-326","313:description:329-391","313:objective:1-57"},["opening"]="Stonegear wanted the inside deck of his siege engine, Trollplow, made more comfortable. Wendigo manes from the Grizzled Den west of Kharanos would furnish the rug he had in mind.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather eight Wendigo Manes for Pilot Stonegear.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Pilot Stonegear with eight Wendigo Manes.",["sourceHash"]="7ea96555117334191a4fda9a208dff6157dc3e3c745071a613d4619ea34940cd",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[314]={["atomIDs"]={"314:description:1-46","314:description:49-110","314:description:113-184","314:description:187-304","314:description:309-372","314:description:375-422","314:description:425-492","314:objective:1-85"},["opening"]="Two rams were missing after cries disturbed the Amberstills' night. Rudra blamed Vagash, the deadly beast above the ranch, and had few soldiers to turn to while Magni's army fought abroad.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Vagash and bring his fang to Rudra.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment against Vagash and delivered his fang to Rudra Amberstill.",["sourceHash"]="98f149351e76aeb892f2515d10cea7e0527e87d0f63cc810542461b40d795dac",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[315]={["atomIDs"]={"315:description:1-50","315:description:53-96","315:description:99-137","315:description:142-222","315:description:225-269","315:description:272-386","315:description:391-485","315:objective:1-66"},["opening"]="Rejold sought a stout unlike any he had brewed before. Frostmane trolls cultivated shimmerweed in the eastern hills; its unusual taste suggested an experiment, if six plants could be obtained from seers or baskets.",["pending"]="{actor} would obtain six Shimmerweeds for Rejold's brewing experiment.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered six Shimmerweeds to Rejold Barleybrew.",["sourceHash"]="f45ed3b075fe46233378049882065be368d9d972c1252d6218979243a19d00e1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[318]={["atomIDs"]={"318:description:1-45","318:description:48-145","318:description:150-246","318:description:249-299","318:description:304-398","318:description:401-465","318:objective:1-67"},["bridge"]="Bellowfiz's provisions still lacked Rejold's Evershine. The brew could warm a traveler or burn in Jetsteam's furnace for a burst of power. Rejold lived west of Kharanos, in Brewnall Village.",["bridgeFrom"]=317,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["editorialReviewRevision"]="whole-route-review-2-2026-10-26",["endingAtomIDs"]={"318:completion:1-37","318:completion:39-53"},["independentReviewRevision"]="r2-findings-applied-2026-10-26",["opening"]="Bellowfiz wanted Evershine for the cold road, but its heat had another use: in a tight moment, he could feed it to Jetsteam's furnace for power. Rejold at Brewnall Village made the potent drink.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to seek a cask of Evershine from Rejold.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="In Brewnall, {actor} found the brewer willing to provide Bellowfiz with Evershine.",["sourceHash"]="cc3dbf5698ad2fde34741a12b71a0aa954d105cb4b672e12e61c19c947a7f781",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[319]={["atomIDs"]={"319:description:1-62","319:description:65-152","319:description:155-182","319:description:187-379","319:objective:1-121"},["bridge"]="Rejold had a cask ready, but asked a favor in return. Bears, boars and leopards strayed close enough to disturb the village's work. Hunting them would leave its craftsmen and brewers more time at their trades.",["bridgeFrom"]=318,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["editorialReviewRevision"]="whole-route-review-2-2026-10-26",["independentReviewRevision"]="r2-findings-applied-2026-10-26",["opening"]="Rejold had Evershine ready, with a favor attached. Bears, boars and leopards wandered close to Brewnall, taking attention away from the villagers' crafts and brewing.",["pending"]="{actor} would meet Rejold's hunting request against six bears, eight elder boars and eight snow leopards.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="Rejold thanked {actor}; fewer growls and snorts outside Brewnall promised more time for the village's trades.",["sourceHash"]="8ac41e47efe533c5ac7a5fd5d0dcf7086dd6ca0f14e8d64e56eb7bec51e19687",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[320]={["aftermath"]="The pilot approved of the brew and considered opening a bottle at once.",["atomIDs"]={"320:description:1-34","320:description:37-81","320:objective:1-68"},["bridge"]="Rejold supplied the promised cask after the hunting around Brewnall. It was ready to join Bellowfiz's provisions at Steelgrill's Depot.",["bridgeFrom"]=319,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["editorialReviewRevision"]="whole-route-review-2-2026-10-26",["endingAtomIDs"]={"320:completion:1-28","320:completion:30-85"},["opening"]="Rejold handed over the cask of Evershine. Its next stop was Steelgrill's Depot, where Pilot Bellowfiz was waiting for the drink.",["pending"]="{actor} would deliver the Evershine to Pilot Bellowfiz.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the cask back to Bellowfiz.",["sourceHash"]="cf1f4c0fc718b423931e2f130fd30512d837cccc2c538e6c099cbb17d6dc3410",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[321]={["atomIDs"]={"321:description:1-132","321:description:137-231","321:description:234-317","321:description:320-361","321:description:383-443","321:description:446-499","321:objective:1-57"},["opening"]="Glorin pointed south of Menethil to the Flying Osprey, an elvish destroyer that carried Lightforge Iron with the Third Fleet. In his account, joining the fleet for protection did not save it from the dragons that sank the ships.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search the Flying Osprey's wreckage for Lightforge Iron.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the search at the Flying Osprey's waterlogged chest.",["sourceHash"]="6bdfb95a12024d7e7a5ef7be6da916d45964f170c5059d13297f891b3bee046e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[322]={["aftermath"]="Grimand welcomed the chance to work Lightforge Iron again. His first task was the weapon; an account of the necromancer's defeat would have to wait.",["atomIDs"]={"322:description:1-103","322:description:106-132","322:description:137-180","322:description:183-224","322:description:227-351","322:objective:1-67"},["bridge"]="The Lightforge Ingots had reached Glorin, but recovering metal was not the same as making a weapon. Packed into a crate, they were bound for Grimand Elmore, the Stormwind smith who could work them.",["bridgeFrom"]=324,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"322:completion:1-30","322:completion:32-51","322:completion:53-98","322:completion:100-142","322:completion:144-229","322:completion:234-263","322:completion:265-305"},["opening"]="The recovered iron was packed for another journey. Glorin knew Grimand Elmore, a weaponsmith in Stormwind's Dwarven District who could work Lightforge Iron into a weapon intended for Morbent Fel.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the Crate of Lightforge Ingots to Grimand Elmore.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the crated Lightforge Ingots to Grimand Elmore.",["sourceHash"]="886ce33fea0ac723f45f5dcaff6c851c9d614ce944f4f8342791af6443dcdcd0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[323]={["atomIDs"]={"323:description:1-61","323:description:64-197","323:description:202-347","323:objective:1-93"},["opening"]="Sven identified Morbent Fel as a necromancer allied with the Dark Riders. Before sending anyone against him, Sven demanded a trial against his skeletal minions: courage alone was no measure of the strength this enemy required.",["pending"]="{actor} would complete Sven's trial against the specified raiders, healers and warders.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Sven's assignment against fifteen Skeletal Raiders, three Skeletal Healers and three Skeletal Warders.",["sourceHash"]="479973e449a3f0a1c41e23e222e3289766728a4db73ce8ba3f523e0f3fd410d0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[324]={["aftermath"]="Glorin accepted the recovered ingots and turned toward making them useful. The Lightforge weapon still lay ahead in the work.",["atomIDs"]={"324:description:1-117","324:description:120-204","324:objective:1-76"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"324:completion:1-19","324:completion:21-90"},["opening"]="A single ingot remained in the broken chest, too little for the weapon needed against Morbent Fel. The rest appeared to have been taken by murlocs near the Flying Osprey; five ingots had to reach Glorin Steelbrow.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover five Lightforge Ingots for Glorin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered five Lightforge Ingots to Glorin Steelbrow.",["sourceHash"]="3fd279302e0a42dfe7f3ed6fb61c9027e6e704345b5c0918319af171511fd79a",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[325]={["aftermath"]="Sven judged the weapon suitable against Morbent Fel. His prediction that the necromancer would fall remained a promise of the confrontation still ahead.",["atomIDs"]={"325:description:1-56","325:description:59-79","325:objective:1-41"},["bridge"]="The iron had reached its craftsman, and Morbent's Bane was ready. The long preparation now led back to Sven and the unfinished struggle above Raven Hill.",["bridgeFrom"]=322,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"325:completion:1-53","325:completion:55-64","325:completion:69-82","325:completion:84-105"},["opening"]="Grimand had provided the weapon meant for the necromancer. Morbent's Bane now had to reach Sven in Duskwood, joining the preparation in Stormwind to the unfinished struggle near Raven Hill.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Morbent's Bane to Sven.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Morbent's Bane to Sven in Duskwood.",["sourceHash"]="d58f80fae57c4d4459102fbf27f3f4e15a9b741bc6191372bec6c46f19ce4081",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[328]={["atomIDs"]={"328:description:1-145","328:description:150-263","328:description:266-361","328:description:366-506","328:objective:1-57"},["bridge"]="The records held no mention of Thorsen, but Herod's ledger concealed a brass key. Notes about a secure strongbox in the Stockpile suggested the papers could still lead to the source of the betrayal.",["bridgeFrom"]=200,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Herod's ledger concealed a brass key but no direct mention of Thorsen. References to a secure strongbox in the Stockpile suggested where the evidence of a leak might instead be locked away.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to use the Small Brass Key on Bookie Herod's Strongbox.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the assignment to open Bookie Herod's Strongbox.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="f259674e565acee60c5e9d7f49dac04afad37742d93928efba5971981e736abf",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[329]={["atomIDs"]={"329:description:1-64","329:description:67-139","329:description:142-233","329:description:236-272","329:description:277-343","329:description:346-406","329:objective:1-58"},["bridge"]="Herod's strongbox had yielded a muddy note rather than a clear name. Its record of Thorsen's routes and contacts, signed with an M, had to be brought to Doren.",["bridgeFrom"]=328,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="A muddy note listed Thorsen's routes, contacts and time among the rebels. Signed only with an M, it suggested an observer close enough to know his daily movements; Doren needed to see that evidence.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take the Muddy Note to Doren.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Muddy Note to Lieutenant Doren.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="16edeb03b757cad0c36dd4308dfd92f15895887b3dd6d470f804440995b28658",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[330]={["atomIDs"]={"330:description:1-80","330:description:85-165","330:description:168-235","330:description:240-262","330:description:265-334","330:objective:1-28"},["bridge"]="The muddy note had reached Doren. Its signature remained obscure, but its author had shared Thorsen's patrol; Sethman's schedules might turn that detail into an identity.",["bridgeFrom"]=329,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="The signature meant little to Doren, but a shared patrol offered a practical lead. Sethman kept the schedules and could identify who had accompanied Thorsen during the relevant week.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to ask Corporal Sethman about Thorsen's patrols.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Corporal Sethman about the patrol schedules.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="e6f4dd6b41b54d1d7edd0066dd826d1d80451ae3d458eba2b33584f54a8f64bd",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[331]={["aftermath"]="Doren identified Merle as the betrayer. Remembering him as a brave soldier made the discovery painful, but removing the secrecy around the spy eased the rebels' danger.",["atomIDs"]={"331:description:1-81","331:objective:1-28"},["bridge"]="The patrol inquiry had reached Sethman. The information now belonged back with Doren, completing the route from the muddy note to the rebel command.",["bridgeFrom"]=330,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"331:completion:1-53","331:completion:55-127","331:completion:129-254"},["opening"]="Sethman directed the patrol information back to the officer who had requested it. The investigation's next step was a report to Doren at the rebel camp.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to return the patrol information to Lieutenant Doren.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported back to Lieutenant Doren.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4e69a83b2d36ac92d0f99b10c29f451cf4c1621d754d2c4f89f84cb5ded32557",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[332]={["atomIDs"]={"332:description:1-92","332:description:95-172","332:description:177-201","332:description:204-297","332:description:300-319","332:objective:1-94"},["opening"]="Renato used a complimentary bottle to draw customers toward the Gallina wine shop. The ticket led along the Trade District canals to his sister Suzetta.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to bring the Wine Ticket to Suzetta.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Wine Ticket to Suzetta Gallina.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="c8a8de27058dc1c48b17838f0754692fc355f87456df4e497cb3b312d084a408",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[333]={["atomIDs"]={"333:description:1-42","333:description:45-102","333:description:105-157","333:description:162-190","333:description:193-259","333:description:262-299","333:description:304-405","333:objective:1-90"},["opening"]="Heavy sales of armor and sturdy clothes had emptied Harlan's knitted stock. Restocking was a more immediate concern than the harsh season he thought his customers feared.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to take Harlan's Cloth Request to Rema Schneider.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Cloth Request to Rema Schneider.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="dafc113202ecc35c7f0b783e0af828d2b3de8f8cb0b521ca3e56cc258616e1a5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[334]={["atomIDs"]={"334:description:1-79","334:description:82-139","334:description:142-262","334:description:267-277","334:description:280-319","334:description:322-437","334:objective:1-100"},["opening"]="Thurman had hurried to his apprenticeship without the shears and needles it required. Rema asked for his sewing kit carried to Larson Clothiers near the Mage's Tower.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to take Thurman's Sewing Kit to him.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Sewing Kit to Thurman Schneider.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="50cb2d1be202bfe69552f92e2763d72fefc5c3d97772f82b74488e916a6d1c70",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[335]={["atomIDs"]={"335:description:1-65","335:description:68-166","335:description:169-237","335:description:243-323","335:description:326-380","335:description:383-506","335:objective:1-116"},["opening"]="Wishock's demand for an investigation threatened Zardeth's hidden establishment. The warlock planned to keep the noble occupied with a preparation requiring a white flower from Darkshire and a root from beneath Stonewrought Dam.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to obtain a Tear of Tilloa and Musquash Root for Zardeth.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Tear of Tilloa and Musquash Root to Zardeth.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="fda8565b2928bea69003f4daac3140870444d5659ac49ffd72bbe98267aae1af",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[336]={["aftermath"]="Wishock accepted the stout and dismissed the messenger so he could enjoy it. The exchange did not itself record the later fate of the noble.",["atomIDs"]={"336:description:1-47","336:description:50-89","336:description:92-119","336:description:122-261","336:description:264-358","336:description:361-386","336:description:391-429","336:description:432-497","336:objective:1-69"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"336:completion:1-63","336:completion:65-88","336:completion:90-142"},["opening"]="Zardeth regarded Wishock's fondness for liquor as useful hypocrisy. The special stout was ready for a noble who denounced the tavern by day and frequented it by night.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to take the Black Claw Stout to Lord Wishock.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Black Claw Stout to Lord Wishock in the Hall of Petitioners.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="f49f7c3a764d772f507b2081dd9af2348844096e5f7378f99300ddb60720d213",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[337]={["atomIDs"]={"337:description:1-146","337:description:149-249","337:description:254-322","337:objective:1-68"},["opening"]="Mud and scratches obscured an old book, but its spine still identified a history of Stormwind. The library seal inside suggested a loan that never found its way back.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return The History of Stormwind to the city library.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned The History of Stormwind to the Stormwind Library.",["sourceHash"]="f7ad914e1944ddc0d34a4d22d2096f9de3f491aa53da0da847dc173867344c41",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[338]={["aftermath"]="Barnil expected the restored book to reach libraries around the world. Recovery of the manuscript made publication possible without establishing that it had already occurred.",["atomIDs"]={"338:description:1-51","338:description:56-144","338:description:147-255","338:description:260-341","338:description:344-399","338:description:404-433","338:description:436-484","338:objective:1-75","338:objective:78-136"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"338:completion:1-48","338:completion:50-74","338:completion:76-172"},["opening"]="Wind scattered the manuscript Barnil had been trusted to proofread. He feared Hemet discovering the loss and offered to organize the recovered pages into the four chapters needed to restore the book.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover and assemble all four manuscript chapters for Barnil.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the four completed chapters of The Green Hills of Stranglethorn to Barnil.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="0bb2bc87bf79f6e6359dec9978a4b3b8393ccead9dc61541ebf3bae174011699",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[339]={["atomIDs"]={"339:description:1-29","339:description:32-139","339:description:145-173","339:description:176-216","339:description:219-291","339:objective:1-126"},["opening"]="The first chapter set out the hunting story's backdrop and companions, including Barnil himself. Its missing pages still lay somewhere in the jungle, leaving four gaps in that introduction.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to gather manuscript pages one, four, six and eight for Barnil.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered pages 1, 4, 6 and 8 to complete the first chapter.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="34cd8a9f71c3c26b6182add4e35027e1c451db7ff9bac265ef2cb998c49f39cb",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[340]={["atomIDs"]={"340:description:1-73","340:description:76-132","340:description:138-233","340:objective:1-130"},["opening"]="The second chapter carried the tales of panther and tiger hunting. Barnil had recovered most of it after the gust, but four pages still prevented the account from being whole.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover manuscript pages ten, eleven, fourteen and sixteen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered pages 10, 11, 14 and 16 to complete the second chapter.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="e4513816b50af63a1152af2a05020589773f27ef0a57e6a46b735f2050c11c3c",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[341]={["atomIDs"]={"341:description:1-28","341:description:31-105","341:description:108-159","341:description:166-247","341:description:250-285","341:objective:1-131"},["opening"]="Barnil favored the third chapter's account of Erlgadin and Rouack using a dwarven rifle. Its cliffhanger still lacked four scattered pages before the chapter could be restored.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to find manuscript pages eighteen, twenty, twenty-one and twenty-four.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered pages 18, 20, 21 and 24 to complete the third chapter.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="64df40a3cd17395ee39b409f513cf6d4294d74d058b3a14912ba0a8dbff3c5d2",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[342]={["atomIDs"]={"342:description:1-30","342:description:33-58","342:description:64-112","342:description:115-174","342:objective:1-127"},["opening"]="Only three pages were missing from the manuscript's finale. Barnil needed that last group to put the fourth chapter back together and preserve its ending.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover manuscript pages twenty-five, twenty-six and twenty-seven.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered pages 25, 26 and 27 to complete the fourth chapter.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8a71b368134b2d898f6da05277e49945ca16b053a219d773f98c2ebbf9b88632",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[343]={["atomIDs"]={"343:description:1-222","343:description:225-251","343:description:254-308","343:description:313-424","343:description:427-472","343:objective:1-70","343:objective:73-158"},["opening"]="Kristoff wanted metallurgy to illuminate a speech about spiritual fortitude. The Royal Library's copy of The Stresses of Iron could supply the passage, if Milton could locate it.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to ask Milton Sheaf for the metallurgy book.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Milton Sheaf at the Royal Library.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8c53d2926b455e395e6b918cbd0d975e54e117239bd1c9a3645fce177a754356",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[344]={["aftermath"]="Paxton admitted he still had the volume and was not ready to release the original before finishing his copy.",["atomIDs"]={"344:description:1-21","344:description:24-44","344:description:47-127","344:description:130-201","344:description:204-216","344:description:221-236","344:description:239-267","344:description:270-323","344:description:326-433","344:description:438-461","344:description:464-502","344:objective:1-50"},["bridge"]="The library inquiry had reached Milton, but the book was absent. Paxton at Northshire had borrowed The Stresses of Iron to copy it months earlier.",["bridgeFrom"]=343,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"344:completion:5-41","344:completion:43-74","344:completion:76-169"},["opening"]="Milton knew the book but no longer had it on his shelves. Paxton had borrowed it months earlier to copy for Northshire Abbey, leaving the librarian puzzled by the delay.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to ask Brother Paxton about The Stresses of Iron.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Brother Paxton at Northshire Abbey.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="6c8b08f2e132f156a8a10159a0c11e151dd10e7fa71da342ca74485054e69a4d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[345]={["aftermath"]="Oslow placed Lakeshire's defense and repairs ahead of the ink errand. The ore would have to be gathered independently.",["atomIDs"]={"345:description:1-67","345:description:72-120","345:description:123-230","345:description:233-340","345:description:345-409","345:description:412-459","345:objective:1-71"},["bridge"]="The borrowed book was still with Paxton. His own fast-drying ink had failed before the copy was complete, sending the errand to Oslow for more Rethban ore.",["bridgeFrom"]=344,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"345:completion:1-15","345:completion:17-135","345:completion:137-197"},["opening"]="Paxton's fast-drying ink had dried before the copying was done. More required Rethban ore, whose usual supplier Oslow lived in Lakeshire.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to ask Foreman Oslow for Rethban Iron Ore.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Foreman Oslow about Paxton's ink supply.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="22c203d384c2c88041e080ed1285070092606a6349008b95615d382dddaf0a4d",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[346]={["atomIDs"]={"346:description:1-78","346:description:81-176","346:objective:1-51","346:objective:54-92"},["bridge"]="The ore had reached Paxton and the copy was finished. The original book could at last return to Kristoff for his speech on fortitude.",["bridgeFrom"]=347,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="The copied volume was finally finished. Paxton released the original for Kristoff's speech and asked that his apology for the long loan reach Milton.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return The Stresses of Iron to Kristoff.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered The Stresses of Iron to Brother Kristoff.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="ea158561c02ab2bdb66b664ce14eeb08ed83e9c208f8169746c2cfb49017d986",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[347]={["aftermath"]="Paxton could now make the dye and finish his copying work. The recovered ore removed the practical cause of the long loan.",["atomIDs"]={"347:description:1-68","347:description:71-182","347:description:185-238","347:description:243-332","347:description:335-454","347:description:459-510","347:objective:1-87"},["bridge"]="The ink request had reached Oslow, who had no ore to spare while Lakeshire prepared for attacks. Five loads from the northern caverns had to be gathered and brought to Paxton directly.",["bridgeFrom"]=345,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"347:completion:1-13","347:completion:15-98","347:completion:103-116"},["opening"]="Rethban ore made weak metal but useful dark dye. Orc preparations had prevented Oslow stocking it, while gnoll drudgers now gathered the mineral in the northern caverns.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring five loads of Rethban Ore to Paxton.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered five loads of Rethban Ore to Brother Paxton.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="c2ffb56e8ca463d461b1216c3e32cf1b02ff78de4fdc22099fb9ca949b29e88b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[348]={["aftermath"]="Fin said strength was returning, though he remained weak and disoriented. The response recorded improvement rather than a claim that every trace of sickness was gone.",["atomIDs"]={"348:description:1-29","348:description:34-93","348:description:98-190","348:description:195-251","348:description:256-305","348:description:310-337","348:objective:1-66","348:objective:68-108"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"348:completion:1-30","348:completion:35-49","348:completion:51-60","348:completion:69-96","348:completion:101-146"},["opening"]="Fin was gravely ill with what he called Stranglethorn Fever. He believed the heart of the elusive Mokk the Savage was the only cure and named Unbagwa, in a southern cape cave, as the witchdoctor able to summon the beast.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to seek Unbagwa's summoning and obtain the Heart of Mokk for Fin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Heart of Mokk to Fin Fizracket.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b7350e1269aa76d097e09fca669271a6392ca41b02fdc6082ce5544554e62fb3",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[349]={["aftermath"]="Unbagwa offered spirit work to draw Mokk the Savage, but demanded protection against other gorillas during it. His promise of a summoning was not a report that Mokk had already appeared.",["atomIDs"]={"349:description:12-53","349:objective:1-32"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"349:completion:1-40","349:completion:42-67","349:completion:69-94","349:completion:99-183"},["opening"]="The errand led to Witch Doctor Unbagwa for a conversation. The terms of his assistance had yet to be stated.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to speak with Witch Doctor Unbagwa.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Witch Doctor Unbagwa.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="16fba49d6dba38917b0b7f0ee8d4bde92676d88389ee69159bd2e70cf71cf98f",["sourceLimitations"]={"Acceptance text states only a conversation; summoning terms appear at progress and completion stages."},["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[350]={["aftermath"]="Trias agreed to hear the whole account despite his irritation at Shaw. He demanded detail rather than a conclusion selected for convenience.",["atomIDs"]={"350:description:1-83","350:description:88-236","350:description:238-319","350:description:321-359","350:description:364-386","350:description:388-451","350:description:453-504","350:objective:1-35"},["bridge"]="Shaw had identified Marzon and his noble employer, but doubted that the remaining evidence could secure proper justice. Elling Trias was the reluctant old contact he now recommended.",["bridgeFrom"]=393,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"350:completion:1-15","350:completion:17-41","350:completion:43-61","350:completion:66-97","350:completion:99-162","350:completion:164-245","350:completion:250-298","350:completion:300-362","350:completion:364-385"},["opening"]="Shaw saw the surviving evidence against Lescovar weakened by the loss of VanCleef and Thredd's testimony. The noble's connections made ordinary justice doubtful, so an old contact in the Trade District offered another approach.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to consult Elling Trias in Stormwind.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Elling Trias.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="25382028bce1d5658f18aae6e030bc6617d1c616561e8013e29ad506235ff358",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[351]={["atomIDs"]={"351:description:1-75","351:description:78-194","351:description:197-249","351:description:254-314","351:description:317-351","351:description:354-390","351:description:393-447","351:description:450-494","351:objective:1-55"},["opening"]="An egg-shaped beacon opened with Oglethorpe's message about a missing robot. The computed crash site lay near Tanaris's Gaping Chasm, where the device was to be carried.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to find OOX-17/TN with the distress beacon.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the distress beacon to Homing Robot OOX-17/TN.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8d594559d2d894c67a106be0846bc0fd93b24a88b4aafd7cd7592266b4bf8b4f",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[353]={["atomIDs"]={"353:description:1-101","353:description:104-211","353:description:216-245","353:description:247-303","353:description:306-380","353:description:385-489","353:objective:1-73"},["opening"]="Grimand had finished a commissioned weapon for the respected Stormpike clan. Its owner was posted far north at Loch Modan's guard tower, leaving delivery between allied homelands still to be arranged.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to deliver the Package for Stormpike.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Package for Stormpike to Mountaineer Stormpike.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="1971c0419b8ff9f42a339e893d58d0c48b07e8da5656e97c0020bdaab58d15d7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[354]={["atomIDs"]={"354:description:1-69","354:description:72-118","354:description:123-252","354:description:255-302","354:description:307-357","354:description:360-399","354:description:404-471","354:description:474-511","354:objective:1-91"},["opening"]="Coleman had worked the mills before the plague. He blamed the Agamands' doomed defense for the undeath of those who stayed beside their employers.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring Coleman three Agamands' remains.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned Gregor's, Nissa's and Thurman's remains to Coleman.",["sourceHash"]="11ffa69f5957ec55cc1834bae4f2ac052b7bd3e6d9beb6e542e4ed19c56b044c",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[355]={["atomIDs"]={"355:description:1-83","355:description:86-157","355:description:162-267","355:objective:1-38"},["bridge"]="Coleman's own grievance had given way to a wider danger at the mills. He told Magistrate Sevren of the work against the Agamands, and the magistrate now wanted to speak with that adventurer.",["bridgeAtomIDs"]={"355:description:1-83","355:description:86-157","355:description:162-267","355:objective:1-38"},["bridgeFrom"]=354,["bridgeMinimumStage"]=2,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["bridgeSourceHash"]="34d420441a8642ca47c7211b87c220c2ff735b3022cc1ec4ddab974b80b0db3e",["independentReviewRevision"]="r2-findings-applied-2026-10-26",["opening"]="Coleman's grievance had become a concern for Brill. The threat still gathered at the mills, and Sevren had asked to meet the person who confronted the family.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to answer Sevren's summons.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} met with Sevren about the mills.",["sourceHash"]="34d420441a8642ca47c7211b87c220c2ff735b3022cc1ec4ddab974b80b0db3e",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[356]={["atomIDs"]={"356:description:1-92","356:description:95-136","356:description:141-294","356:description:299-317","356:description:320-361","356:description:364-423","356:description:426-471","356:objective:1-88"},["opening"]="The Bulwark's defenders faced the Plaguelands, but enemies slipping behind them threatened their supply line. Linnea directed attention toward Balnir Farmstead.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to patrol against the horrors and spirits.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported completion of Linnea's rear patrol.",["sourceHash"]="f5748a7a09225ef297c95de3920d3f7d448f50dcc8c13bd5b424ba3118f380f9",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[357]={["aftermath"]="Bethor recognized Gunther, his old companion, and judged from the book that his power had grown since death.",["atomIDs"]={"357:description:1-74","357:description:77-216","357:description:221-272","357:description:275-359","357:description:364-430","357:description:433-486","357:objective:1-63"},["bridge"]="Bethor's mission concerned a lich on Brightwater Lake who attacked those approaching him. The isolated Forsaken believed other undead were still slaves; his spellbook could reveal both his identity and the powers the Queen might gain.",["bridgeAtomIDs"]={"357:description:1-74","357:description:77-216","357:description:221-272","357:description:275-359","357:description:364-430","357:description:433-486","357:objective:1-63"},["bridgeFrom"]=405,["bridgeMinimumStage"]=2,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["bridgeSourceHash"]="2e7415c68edbdd92878cd5776d7c3577d0298ca7d5bd3928b2bb1792979ffe23",["endingAtomIDs"]={"357:completion:1-14","357:completion:16-78","357:completion:80-111","357:completion:116-182","357:completion:187-198","357:completion:200-267","357:completion:272-376","357:completion:378-444","357:completion:449-487"},["opening"]="Bethor wanted to identify a free-willed lich who mistook all other undead for Scourge slaves. The spellbook could reveal both his name and the abilities the Queen might recruit.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover the lich's book.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered it to Bethor.",["sourceHash"]="2e7415c68edbdd92878cd5776d7c3577d0298ca7d5bd3928b2bb1792979ffe23",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[358]={["aftermath"]="Sevren directed the ichor toward apothecary study, where it might reveal a weapon against the Scourge.",["atomIDs"]={"358:description:1-165","358:description:172-334","358:description:337-359","358:description:364-504","358:objective:1-49","358:objective:56-110"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"358:completion:1-18","358:completion:20-185","358:completion:187-230","358:completion:235-255","358:completion:257-372"},["opening"]="Tirisfal's mass graves held victims who had so far remained dead. Rot Hide gnolls were gathering those bodies to strengthen the Scourge's armies.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to stop the graverobbers and gather ichor.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Sevren's assignment against the Rot Hides.",["sourceHash"]="7c3638dc209abb8f3c3dda4bb2e067720eca598ab527860c47646dfcd8ed7474",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[359]={["aftermath"]="Linnea reported scattered incursions beyond the Bulwark, with a concentration around Balnir Farmstead.",["atomIDs"]={"359:description:1-65","359:description:70-152","359:description:155-276","359:description:281-349","359:description:352-380","359:description:383-413","359:objective:1-29"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"359:completion:1-33","359:completion:35-159","359:completion:164-273"},["opening"]="Sevren needed fresh news from the eastern waystation. Even a border holding most enemies back could leave Tirisfal exposed to those who slipped through.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to obtain Linnea's report.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reached Linnea at the waystation.",["sourceHash"]="b07dc0027d976b7e05f8f2983376ab62a0f1c9f4e931ad8716c3aeeb8fc4ce59",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[360]={["atomIDs"]={"360:description:1-64","360:description:67-113","360:description:118-227","360:objective:1-37"},["opening"]="Linnea's information was ready for the return to Brill. Sevren had requested news from the border and needed it promptly.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to relay the waystation's information.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} relayed Linnea's information to Sevren.",["sourceHash"]="a14a517bb49944a6489eca12ec53701ba1f361c7e7154fd874454a9e30b9364f",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[361]={["aftermath"]="Yvette recalled begging Thurman to leave. She acknowledged their former love, then declared that life ended.",["atomIDs"]={"361:description:1-70","361:description:73-159","361:objective:1-73"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"361:completion:1-21","361:completion:23-119","361:completion:121-134","361:completion:136-177","361:completion:179-217","361:completion:222-266","361:completion:271-299","361:completion:301-360","361:completion:362-456","361:completion:461-482","361:completion:484-491"},["opening"]="Thurman's letter bore Yvette's name but appeared never to have reached her. The undelivered message offered one remaining connection across the fall of the mills.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to find Yvette and carry the letter to her.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Thurman's letter to Yvette.",["sourceHash"]="1048bb601a24ab96b77774b87e404d389727436798bfcca959c0e3de1aa65c5d",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[362]={["atomIDs"]={"362:description:1-114","362:description:117-197","362:description:202-301","362:description:304-384","362:description:389-455","362:description:458-503","362:objective:1-77"},["opening"]="Coleman remembered Devlin as the sharp-tongued younger Agamand son. The fallen son's chatter could still be heard near the road to the mills.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover Devlin's remains for Coleman.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned Devlin's remains to Coleman.",["sourceHash"]="288b7cb0ef0d616cd6a444bd7ac0f036c4c4fa71d84858ace6f9478134add1e0",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[366]={["aftermath"]="Gunther recognized Bethor's spell and began to consider that his former companion might also be free.",["atomIDs"]={"366:description:1-159","366:description:164-287","366:description:290-319","366:description:324-340","366:description:343-449","366:description:452-506","366:objective:1-70"},["bridge"]="The book led Bethor back to Gunther, a friend he had thought lost. An enchantment would carry proof of Bethor's own freedom from the Lich King, opening a way to approach the old comrade through recognition.",["bridgeAtomIDs"]={"366:description:1-159","366:description:164-287","366:description:290-319","366:description:324-340","366:description:343-449","366:description:452-506","366:objective:1-70"},["bridgeFrom"]=357,["bridgeMinimumStage"]=2,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["bridgeSourceHash"]="21b9adc98b126a046d74e2343a80c121899bbd03f17e0288a234563d8a5aaa2e",["endingAtomIDs"]={"366:completion:1-10","366:completion:12-46","366:completion:51-102","366:completion:104-122","366:completion:127-203"},["opening"]="Bethor recognized Gunther as an old Kirin Tor companion who had escaped domination. His enchantment on the spellbook was meant to reveal that he too was free.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return the enchanted book to Gunther.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the spellbook to Gunther.",["sourceHash"]="21b9adc98b126a046d74e2343a80c121899bbd03f17e0288a234563d8a5aaa2e",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[373]={["aftermath"]="Baros read the letter as the work of an idealist consumed by revenge. His judgment mixed criticism of VanCleef's victims with an unwillingness to dismiss the grievance behind them.",["atomIDs"]={"373:description:1-86","373:description:88-183","373:description:188-232","373:objective:1-72"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"373:completion:1-24","373:completion:26-84","373:completion:86-111","373:completion:113-160","373:completion:162-208","373:completion:210-283","373:completion:288-314","373:completion:319-326","373:completion:328-406","373:completion:408-440","373:completion:442-466","373:completion:468-506"},["opening"]="An unsent, sealed letter remained among VanCleef's belongings. Its address named Stormwind's city architect, Baros Alexston, making City Hall the destination for a message that had never left its author.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the Letter to the City Architect to Baros.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the letter to Baros Alexston.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="149aaeed8ef8951d80d85525bb8fa3e9e9fdd66913d07c7f2ad7c9cae399c118",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[377]={["atomIDs"]={"377:description:1-256","377:description:261-353","377:description:356-399","377:description:404-491","377:objective:1-82"},["opening"]="Darkshire's council resented Stormwind keeping Ward imprisoned rather than honoring its death sentence. Millstipe accused him of selling cemetery bodies to Morbent Fel and demanded a hand as proof of execution inside the Stockade.",["pending"]="{actor} would recover Dextren Ward's hand for Millstipe.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the hand of Dextren Ward to Councilman Millstipe.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="4502e1273d84d4d5bd96674b3f9e43efc1d00f8f2591f7ab660015d8ff8fc3b5",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[378]={["atomIDs"]={"378:description:1-47","378:description:50-110","378:description:115-203","378:description:206-318","378:description:321-378","378:description:383-453","378:description:456-475","378:description:478-491","378:description:494-511","378:objective:1-69"},["opening"]="Garmason's loyalty kept him beside Longbraid while intelligence identified a conspirator in the span's destruction. Kam Deepfury was held in Stormwind, beyond the immediate reach of the dwarves whose kin the plan had killed.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring Kam Deepfury's head to Garmason.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Kam Deepfury's head to Motley Garmason.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="6830ddc9c492b48a196788fc266a6cd73903ec21eb5acb02c7b7b5ddece02f41",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[379]={["atomIDs"]={"379:description:1-24","379:description:27-51","379:description:54-70","379:description:73-98","379:description:101-172","379:description:177-182","379:description:184-234","379:description:237-332","379:description:335-373","379:objective:1-78"},["bridge"]="The power-source inquiry had reached Bilgewhizzle. His terms were five Wastewander water pouches before the testing kit could receive the 4711-FTZ.",["bridgeFrom"]=243,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="Bilgewhizzle could supply the needed 4711-FTZ, but thirst set his price. Five water pouches from the Wastewander nomads east of Gadgetzan were his demand for a power source.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to obtain five Wastewander Water Pouches for Bilgewhizzle.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered five Wastewander Water Pouches to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="bc07f39b8cd482dd405c5cebe383559386f059a51100d2493f2cfdb0d71522e4",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[385]={["atomIDs"]={"385:description:1-66","385:description:68-210","385:description:215-353","385:description:355-449","385:description:454-474","385:objective:1-97"},["opening"]="Crocolisks drew hunters to Loch Modan and supplied both leatherworkers and tables. Marek said their island strongholds made the trade a dangerous one, and requested meat and skins for the Farstrider Lodge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather five Crocolisk Meats and six Crocolisk Skins for Marek.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Marek Ironheart with five pieces of Crocolisk Meat and six Crocolisk Skins.",["sourceHash"]="4724b7f3e82f91e61af50b9f70f9713d978e9c5c0b6970afa439b46cb932c687",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[386]={["atomIDs"]={"386:description:1-66","386:description:69-124","386:description:127-197","386:description:200-264","386:description:267-289","386:description:292-350","386:description:353-388","386:description:393-428","386:description:431-495","386:objective:1-65"},["opening"]="Targorr's execution had been delayed by a noble, alarming Berton. The guard remembered the orc's torture of captured defenders and suspected foul play behind the bureaucratic pause.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover Targorr the Dread's head from the Stockade.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Targorr the Dread's head to Guard Berton.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="a38611f9b241e21d14873caf3309af55433e13e0c26a4d1e3ba00e8088dca48b",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[387]={["atomIDs"]={"387:description:1-29","387:description:32-54","387:description:57-119","387:description:122-171","387:description:174-269","387:description:274-312","387:description:315-342","387:description:345-383","387:objective:1-128"},["opening"]="Thelwater feared both an overrun prison and the loss of his post. He ordered a lethal response against three ranks of Defias prisoners to reassert control over the Stockade.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront ten Defias Prisoners, eight Convicts and eight Insurgents.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Thelwater's assignment against the specified Defias prisoners.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b77fd59028270cb1b772070b138a5c300b97e18c24d9badf2384e8d1b4b12acb",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[388]={["atomIDs"]={"388:description:1-52","388:description:55-92","388:description:95-114","388:description:117-193","388:description:196-262","388:description:265-374","388:description:377-413","388:description:418-432","388:description:435-478","388:description:481-508","388:objective:1-69"},["opening"]="Nikova's fourteen-year-old grandson had guarded the Stockade while the army fought elsewhere. She said prisoners killed him for challenging their gang scarves, and sought ten wool bandanas as a grandmother's revenge.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring ten Red Wool Bandanas to Nikova.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten Red Wool Bandanas to Nikova Raskol.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="baee3b1d8241bb27e9f8a43472b59af548249a99f5380bf048c50dee8fcf2314",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[389]={["aftermath"]="Thelwater's Stockade was already in crisis, with open cells and a riot linked to Thredd. The inquiry reached a prison that could not offer a quiet interview.",["atomIDs"]={"389:description:1-53","389:description:55-110","389:description:115-163","389:description:165-206","389:description:208-344","389:description:346-395","389:description:400-468","389:description:470-510","389:objective:1-44"},["bridge"]="Baros remembered the Stonemasons' unpaid work rebuilding Stormwind. Bazil Thredd, now in the Stockade, might know how VanCleef's grievance had become a plan for revenge.",["bridgeFrom"]=373,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"389:completion:1-30","389:completion:32-67","389:completion:72-85","389:completion:87-132","389:completion:134-229","389:completion:231-306"},["opening"]="Baros remembered the rebuilding of Stormwind and the Stonemasons' unpaid work. In his account, VanCleef rejected a government post, led a riot and swore revenge; the imprisoned Bazil Thredd might know the resulting plans.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Warden Thelwater about Thredd.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} consulted Warden Thelwater in the Stockade.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="73bfdf066e57bcaf71594b5e6813863f134f8a247111db521b64bf8430e1e0f1",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[391]={["atomIDs"]={"391:description:1-52","391:description:54-124","391:description:129-205","391:description:207-292","391:description:294-354","391:description:356-419","391:objective:1-78"},["bridge"]="The inquiry reached a prison already in revolt. Thelwater demanded proof against Thredd before he would trust the visitor's professed allegiance.",["bridgeFrom"]=389,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["opening"]="The warden distrusted the visitor but allowed an entry into the riot. A head brought back from Thredd was his condition for believing the professed allegiance.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to confront Bazil Thredd and return his head to Thelwater.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Thredd assignment and delivered his head to Warden Thelwater.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8471649e1a584af1309f6b5ad7d46a561493fab65b20c1836d0ee90085519bc7",["sourceMapID"]="?",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[392]={["aftermath"]="Baros recognized neither the name nor description and kept several possible affiliations open. He needed another person's knowledge before identifying the visitor.",["atomIDs"]={"392:description:1-75","392:description:77-157","392:description:162-240","392:description:242-266","392:description:268-304","392:description:306-357","392:description:362-427","392:description:429-482","392:objective:1-80"},["bridge"]="Thredd's recent visitor was the new lead: a quiet man whose papers named him Maelik. A sealed description could carry that uncertainty back to the architect.",["bridgeFrom"]=391,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"392:completion:1-4","392:completion:6-12","392:completion:14-83","392:completion:85-108","392:completion:110-162","392:completion:164-261","392:completion:263-275"},["opening"]="Thredd had gone years without visitors before a quiet man began calling regularly. Thelwater's suspicions found no fault in papers naming him Maelik, but a description could still be carried back for examination.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring the Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor to Baros.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor to Baros Alexston.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="8519baeb606b428f0f8526bfcb8aaa173d05deb44c3014edbde4b509d5d14ce9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[393]={["aftermath"]="Shaw recognized the visitor under another alias, Marzon, while doubting that name was genuine either. He identified the assassin's current employer as Lord Gregor Lescovar.",["atomIDs"]={"393:description:1-28","393:description:30-159","393:description:161-229","393:description:231-307","393:description:312-340","393:objective:1-85"},["bridge"]="The visitor's description had reached Baros without a recognition. He sent it to Shaw, whose knowledge of concealed city dealings might supply an identity.",["bridgeFrom"]=392,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"393:completion:1-5","393:completion:7-18","393:completion:20-86","393:completion:88-175","393:completion:177-275","393:completion:280-342","393:completion:347-491"},["opening"]="Baros could not identify the visitor. Shaw's knowledge of Stormwind's concealed dealings, and a favor owed, made SI:7 the next place for the sealed description.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the visitor's description to Mathias Shaw.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Sealed Description of Thredd's Visitor to Master Mathias Shaw.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="59f58bfecee8d676ecc841f73ff3320797ab31c1979f666125dbd11ded74bea3",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[394]={["aftermath"]="Shaw accepted the news of the death and thanked the messenger for service to Stormwind. His response acknowledged the result without detailing an unseen blow.",["atomIDs"]={"394:description:1-22","394:description:24-145","394:description:147-218","394:description:223-302","394:description:304-337","394:description:339-435","394:objective:1-35"},["bridge"]="The garden operation had ended and Trias had received its result. He sent the outcome back to Shaw in Old Town before the investigation passed toward court.",["bridgeFrom"]=434,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"394:completion:1-17","394:completion:19-45","394:completion:47-98","394:completion:103-144","394:completion:149-172","394:completion:174-220","394:completion:222-316"},["opening"]="Trias sent the outcome of the Lescovar affair back to Shaw. His warning about noble power accompanied a report he expected might earn attention at court.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to report to Mathias Shaw.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Mathias Shaw about the Lescovar affair.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="602d3b26db9c8cd517ec32f523fb52fd70cfedf61bf5cab3b6ee3478ac5d861b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[395]={["aftermath"]="Baros had heard Lescovar was found dead and counted the mission successful. He believed the result protected many people from VanCleef's revenge.",["atomIDs"]={"395:description:1-20","395:description:22-84","395:description:86-168","395:description:173-288","395:description:290-298","395:description:308-320","395:description:322-350","395:description:355-411","395:description:413-419","395:description:421-439","395:objective:1-39"},["bridge"]="The report had reached Shaw. Baros now wished to speak, while Shaw urged continued silence about Trias and care in describing Lescovar's death.",["bridgeFrom"]=394,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"395:completion:1-25","395:completion:27-93","395:completion:98-152","395:completion:154-240"},["opening"]="Shaw directed another meeting with Baros while urging discretion about Lescovar and Trias. The investigation's public account would pass through the architect without every hidden participant being named.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to speak with Baros Alexston again.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Baros Alexston.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="f5b00e83b61a411a9ef28341397ef2452e3a14dcbf2639a59635266f029f5bf9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[396]={["aftermath"]="Prestor conveyed royal appreciation while explaining that the king was away on a diplomatic mission. The audience therefore ended through a representative rather than an encounter with the absent monarch.",["atomIDs"]={"396:description:1-38","396:description:40-132","396:description:134-237","396:description:242-334","396:objective:1-97"},["bridge"]="Baros had received the account and prepared a Defias report for royal attention. The next audience belonged at Stormwind Keep, where the findings were to be conveyed.",["bridgeFrom"]=395,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"396:completion:1-72","396:completion:74-223","396:completion:228-280","396:completion:282-408"},["opening"]="Baros had prepared the Defias report for royal attention. The bearer was to add an account of the findings at Stormwind Keep, where the audience had been arranged.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to deliver Baros's Defias report at Stormwind Keep.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the Defias report audience at Stormwind Keep.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceConflicts"]={"Objective names King Varian; finisher metadata names Lady Katrana Prestor and completion says king absent. No personal encounter with Varian asserted."},["sourceHash"]="3ef0d6bf56ed36c89369dcf391521db25def2f6b9c992410c6ee72895915d764",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[397]={["aftermath"]="Zggi followed the master's command despite wanting to keep the gift. The servant's response completed the promised reward exchange.",["atomIDs"]={"397:description:1-41","397:description:48-75","397:description:78-172","397:description:175-231","397:description:234-284","397:objective:1-76"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"397:completion:1-28","397:completion:30-102"},["opening"]="Zardeth credited the served drink with freeing Stormwind's warlocks from Wishock's interference. A gift waited with his servant Zggi, marking the establishment's satisfaction with the completed errand.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to speak with Zggi at Zardeth's request.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Zggi.",["sourceClassMask"]="256",["sourceHash"]="92d66cd704bfae019677bc55137fc7fe6de8c244f80e919a7ce33c5c57dd89ae",["sourceRaceMask"]="65",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[399]={["aftermath"]="The recovered compass had no practical value to Baros, but its childhood associations mattered. Its return preserved a personal connection the burned farm could no longer supply.",["atomIDs"]={"399:description:1-68","399:description:70-115","399:description:117-204","399:description:209-306","399:description:308-334","399:description:336-401","399:description:406-462","399:description:464-507","399:objective:1-124"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"399:completion:1-18","399:completion:20-79","399:completion:81-133","399:completion:135-238","399:completion:240-300"},["opening"]="Baros's childhood farm had burned and passed into thieves' hands. His father believed the first compass remained hidden there, offering the architect a chance to recover one small object from a vanished home.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover Baros's compass from the Alexston Farmstead.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the compass to Baros Alexston.",["sourceClassMask"]="?",["sourceHash"]="b656b118a96da2c1f4d61aabbdda561d58bbaae6efa9d9e47b159c4d8318738e",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[400]={["atomIDs"]={"400:description:1-93","400:description:96-131","400:description:134-209","400:description:214-253","400:description:256-320","400:description:325-384","400:description:387-502","400:objective:1-48"},["opening"]="Steelgrill's work was hard on his tools, and Tharek had filled another order for the mechanic. The delivery went northeast of Kharanos to a depot frequented by veteran siege-engine pilots.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take Steelgrill's Tools to Beldin Steelgrill.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the tool order to Beldin Steelgrill.",["sourceHash"]="ce1f9910e687ce1d355645aa697b3dba0bf38af18e8f1d717c82caf75ce8272b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[401]={["aftermath"]="Sirra finished the translation. The source described the air growing oppressive as the completed message became available.",["atomIDs"]={"401:description:1-42","401:description:45-95","401:objective:1-52"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"401:completion:1-13","401:completion:16-33","401:completion:38-114"},["opening"]="Sirra's translation was nearly finished. The message still required a little time before its meaning could be reported.",["pending"]="{actor} would wait briefly and speak with Sirra again.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Sirra after the translation was finished.",["sourceHash"]="641200de4ce6cdce459b91cc55e90f5bb756e8ba9220fde2daba371055d0f203",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[405]={["atomIDs"]={"405:description:1-152","405:description:155-182","405:description:187-217","405:description:220-261","405:description:264-333","405:description:336-360","405:description:365-386","405:description:389-406","405:description:411-468","405:objective:1-60"},["bridge"]="The new orders came from Bethor in the Undercity. Sevren wanted proven service against the Scourge turned toward a dangerous recruitment, leaving the wayward lich and the mission's particulars to the mage.",["bridgeAtomIDs"]={"405:description:1-152","405:description:155-182","405:description:187-217","405:description:220-261","405:description:264-333","405:description:336-360","405:description:365-386","405:description:389-406","405:description:411-468","405:objective:1-60"},["bridgeFrom"]=358,["bridgeMinimumStage"]=2,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["bridgeSourceHash"]="eb7062ff5d382ea2d38d62b975e8bc803e0bcf43b7ef3ca1baec1fd73cbd5425",["opening"]="Bethor had requested an agent of proven worth for a dangerous recruitment. Sevren knew only that the assignment concerned a wayward lich.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to present Sevren's orders to Bethor.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} presented the orders to Bethor.",["sourceHash"]="eb7062ff5d382ea2d38d62b975e8bc803e0bcf43b7ef3ca1baec1fd73cbd5425",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[407]={["aftermath"]="The captive welcomed the pumpkin as long-awaited food.",["atomIDs"]={"407:description:1-25","407:description:28-47","407:description:50-212","407:description:217-292","407:description:295-369","407:description:374-477","407:description:480-509","407:objective:1-113"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"407:completion:1-13","407:completion:16-33","407:completion:36-56"},["opening"]="Johaan had laced a pumpkin with his latest formula. A Scarlet captive beneath the tavern was to receive the preparation as food.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to take Johaan's pumpkin to the prisoner.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the laced pumpkin to the captive.",["sourceHash"]="2bd367a4ca11788e71f31e8aa515139ce42cfecc8ea701df946f0bcda05557d1",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[408]={["atomIDs"]={"408:description:1-61","408:description:64-199","408:description:202-294","408:description:299-337","408:description:340-414","408:description:419-460","408:objective:1-49","408:objective:54-124"},["bridge"]="Sevren's concern led from the family above ground to its ancestors below. Dargol had made the crypt a Scourge headquarters and raised the dead Agamands to fight for him.",["bridgeAtomIDs"]={"408:description:1-61","408:description:64-199","408:description:202-294","408:description:299-337","408:description:340-414","408:description:419-460","408:objective:1-49","408:objective:54-124"},["bridgeFrom"]=355,["bridgeMinimumStage"]=2,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["bridgeSourceHash"]="c5872f4277712947be70f3a0f9f3eb136b08038928e6a7dafff14a910262f653",["opening"]="Sevren identified the crypt as the Scourge's strongest position at the mills. Captain Dargol had raised the ancestors there and planned to use them against the Forsaken.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to break Dargol's force and recover his skull.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled Sevren's assignment at the family crypt.",["sourceHash"]="c5872f4277712947be70f3a0f9f3eb136b08038928e6a7dafff14a910262f653",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[409]={["aftermath"]="Gunther accepted that other undead had broken the Lich King's domination.",["atomIDs"]={"409:description:1-121","409:description:124-200","409:description:205-277","409:description:280-334","409:description:339-386","409:description:389-433","409:description:436-499","409:objective:1-29","409:objective:34-68","409:objective:73-104"},["bridge"]="Bethor's enchantment gave Gunther a reason to listen, but he still wanted proof of opposition to the Scourge. A candle at Lillith's altar would call forth the enemy he required the visitor to face.",["bridgeAtomIDs"]={"409:description:1-121","409:description:124-200","409:description:205-277","409:description:280-334","409:description:339-386","409:description:389-433","409:description:436-499","409:objective:1-29","409:objective:34-68","409:objective:73-104"},["bridgeFrom"]=366,["bridgeMinimumStage"]=2,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["bridgeSourceHash"]="90ec6819e62c17a47cf4895c3414c90306510d6ea81551a90b61c6e613b13c14",["endingAtomIDs"]={"409:completion:1-74","409:completion:76-86","409:completion:91-225"},["opening"]="The book's enchantment supported the claim of freedom, but Gunther demanded another proof. Defeating the agent called at the bloody altar would establish hostility to the Scourge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to face Lillith as Gunther's test.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Gunther after fulfilling his test.",["sourceHash"]="90ec6819e62c17a47cf4895c3414c90306510d6ea81551a90b61c6e613b13c14",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[411]={["aftermath"]="Bethor received the gem as proof of Gunther's allegiance and planned to inform the Dark Lady.",["atomIDs"]={"411:description:1-46","411:description:49-78","411:description:80-107","411:objective:1-57"},["bridge"]="Gunther now had a message for his old comrade. A Nether Gem would let the two speak, and Bethor in the Undercity was to receive it.",["bridgeAtomIDs"]={"411:description:1-46","411:description:49-78","411:description:80-107","411:objective:1-57"},["bridgeFrom"]=409,["bridgeMinimumStage"]=2,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["bridgeSourceHash"]="a7ce8f6fb6b7bffa8bf30a104374fd76778cb5fcb9247a178608be9d3471e0fb",["endingAtomIDs"]={"411:completion:1-29","411:completion:31-78","411:completion:80-110"},["opening"]="Gunther entrusted a Nether Gem to the journey back to Bethor. The object would let old companions speak across the distance.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to carry the gem to the Undercity.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered Gunther's gem to Bethor.",["sourceHash"]="a7ce8f6fb6b7bffa8bf30a104374fd76778cb5fcb9247a178608be9d3471e0fb",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[412]={["atomIDs"]={"412:description:1-223","412:description:228-327","412:description:330-436","412:description:439-505","412:objective:1-86"},["opening"]="Razzle described the attempt to clear Gnomeregan as a disaster that left gnomes transformed into lepers. He and Ozzie hoped a Recombobulator could reverse the effect, but their unfinished machine lacked cogs and gears from outside the city.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover eight Restabilization Cogs and eight Gyromechanic Gears for Razzle.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the eight cogs and eight gears requested by Razzle Sprysprocket.",["sourceHash"]="f918d1a33f85ba9e2fd5ab9d29257aa8a2d2cb94c342e16a70a6017488b8e604",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[413]={["atomIDs"]={"413:description:1-56","413:description:59-162","413:description:167-277","413:description:282-335","413:objective:1-59"},["opening"]="Rejold wanted his brother Wellart to taste the new Shimmer Stout. The brewer's family connection followed a barrel to the southern guard tower on the Loch Modan border.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to take the Barrel of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Barleybrew.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Barrel of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Barleybrew.",["sourceHash"]="911b6bd59a1d938a7aa0ba0e80b47aee18818c1ed36eb283deeebe4b7dc34109",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[414]={["atomIDs"]={"414:description:1-81","414:description:84-121","414:description:124-212","414:description:217-322","414:description:325-365","414:description:370-444","414:objective:1-54"},["opening"]="Wellart wanted another mountaineer to share his brother's stout. Kadrell patrolled the road through Thelsamar, beyond the tunnel into Loch Modan, and a cask was set aside for him.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to carry the Cask of Shimmer Stout to Kadrell.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the Cask of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Kadrell.",["sourceHash"]="8ce741c5be37a91a404b04bcbd1f7ee7cd143e569aca3700f1fd8a8d52eeb739",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[415]={["atomIDs"]={"415:description:1-62","415:description:67-173","415:description:176-250","415:description:255-301","415:objective:1-29"},["opening"]="Tharek passed on word that Rejold had been asking for a visitor at Brewnall Village. The brewer wanted to discuss a new drink and the help it might need.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to return to Brewnall Village to speak with Rejold.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Rejold Barleybrew about his new brew.",["sourceHash"]="34a34a0d78adc7d4e684ffa6d05a121c257bdc345263992b28b547e11365dc02",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[416]={["atomIDs"]={"416:description:1-47","416:description:50-153","416:description:158-181","416:description:184-236","416:description:241-338","416:objective:1-61"},["opening"]="Tunnel rat kobolds had established dens along the mountainside west of Thelsamar. Kadrell offered bounties for their ears as part of the effort to clear the foothills.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring twelve Tunnel Rat Ears to Kadrell.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered twelve Tunnel Rat Ears to Mountaineer Kadrell.",["sourceHash"]="99f5d53fce458b00a8eccbc3d77b576eb45e5668d9e23b64e7d64e48c3e23e03",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[417]={["atomIDs"]={"417:description:1-152","417:description:157-249","417:description:254-312","417:description:317-342","417:objective:1-15","417:objective:20-83"},["opening"]="Hildelve's journal named Mangeclaw as the bear that mauled him, and the state of his body suggested the beast returned. His final written wish was revenge; the journal and a claw were to go to Hammerfoot.",["pending"]="{actor} would confront Mangeclaw and bring the claw and Hildelve's journal to Hammerfoot.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} fulfilled the assignment against Mangeclaw and delivered the Mangy Claw and Hildelve's Journal to Hammerfoot.",["sourceHash"]="c9915170b97f1b8ed4350fae5e08d05a819803ff3d9edb829a0e070131cc63bb",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[418]={["atomIDs"]={"418:description:1-149","418:description:151-226","418:description:235-359","418:description:364-444","418:description:446-502","418:objective:1-101"},["opening"]="Vidra fed Thelsamar's children and workers returning from the excavation. Her blood sausages needed bear meat, boar intestines for casings and spider ichor for seasoning; even a traveler had to contribute to the kitchen.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to gather three portions each of Bear Meat, Boar Intestines and Spider Ichor for Vidra.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} supplied Vidra Hearthstove with the three requested portions of each sausage ingredient.",["sourceHash"]="f8a4682a45a66a6f38203f9431a205a6bd59abbc41a85e484e58095da0bb4feb",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[419]={["atomIDs"]={"419:description:1-77","419:description:80-226","419:description:231-358","419:description:363-435","419:description:438-476","419:description:481-491","419:description:494-502","419:objective:1-20"},["opening"]="A search for ore left two siege engines stranded and Hildelve continuing alone on foot. Days had passed without his return, and Hammerfoot had heard beasts in the hills at night.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to search the hills for Pilot Hildelve.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} located Pilot Hildelve.",["sourceHash"]="5835b92fc4e48f512c39269181adff4c8795ca60cebfafd4af3e7dad257f5693",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[421]={["atomIDs"]={"421:description:1-102","421:description:107-281","421:description:286-361","421:description:364-418","421:description:421-498","421:objective:1-75"},["opening"]="Sylvanas had charged Varimathras with expansion into human and dwarven lands to the south. Dalar regarded Arugal's curse as an obstacle in strategic Silverpine and demanded a combat trial against the whitescalps.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to confront five whitescalps.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Dalar's trial against the whitescalps.",["sourceHash"]="2bd29c0b15a3cd5d80c45e76e609f8c25e6dda5410c6c6a1dd018257b5323179",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
